00:10:39,458 --> 00:10:40,507
- [Joel] Boy, they're sure tough

244
00:10:40,507 --> 00:10:41,677
on drunk drivers in Canada.

245
00:10:41,677 --> 00:10:44,010
(whistling)

246
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:50,310
- [Voiceover] Johnny is invited
to help put on the show,

247
00:10:50,310 --> 00:10:52,585
and don't thin he doesn't enjoy himself.

248
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:53,488
- [Joel] That's a guy!

249
00:10:53,488 --> 00:10:54,945
- [Voiceover] The only
problem is afterwards,

250
00:10:54,945 --> 00:10:57,339
Johnny can't stop going up and down.

251
00:10:57,339 --> 00:10:58,672
- [Crow] The drugs from
the Chemical Wonderland

252
00:10:58,672 --> 00:11:00,089
start to kick in.

253
00:11:02,090 --> 00:11:03,246
(laughing)

254
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:05,354
- [Voiceover] Johnny's mother
is still trying to find her

255
00:11:05,354 --> 00:11:08,024
missing son and thinks she
might see Johnny on the edge

256
00:11:08,024 --> 00:11:09,373
of the crowd gathered to hear the former

257
00:11:09,373 --> 00:11:11,351
Prime Minister of Canada,
- [Joel] Yeah, right.

258
00:11:11,351 --> 00:11:13,064
Mr. McKenzie King.

259
00:11:13,064 --> 00:11:15,419
She never dreams her
Johnny is on the platform

260
00:11:15,419 --> 00:11:18,155
discussing the situation
with the guest speaker.

261
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:19,587
- [Joel] Tell me Johnny,
now what do you think

262
00:11:19,587 --> 00:11:21,186
of the new free trade agreement?

263
00:11:21,186 --> 00:11:24,491
- [Tom] I have to go, horsies.

264
00:11:24,491 --> 00:11:25,406
- [Crow] The hell was his name again?

265
00:11:25,406 --> 00:11:27,435
Jimmy, no, Jerry...

266
00:11:27,435 --> 00:11:29,727
- [Voiceover] Johnny gets an
escort down from the platform

267
00:11:29,727 --> 00:11:31,745
and is off again.

268
00:11:31,745 --> 00:11:33,226
- [Crow] It will be the
first of many encounters with

269
00:11:33,226 --> 00:11:35,054
bouncers for Johnny.

270
00:11:35,054 --> 00:11:37,221
(honking)

271
00:11:40,226 --> 00:11:41,291
- [Voiceover] Oh boy,

272
00:11:41,291 --> 00:11:43,458
a helicopter airplane.
- [Joel] What?

273
00:11:43,458 --> 00:11:44,893
Jimminy, thinks Johnny,

274
00:11:44,893 --> 00:11:47,009
if only I can get a ride in one of those.

275
00:11:47,009 --> 00:11:48,404
- [Tom] Visions of the Mekong Delta

276
00:11:48,404 --> 00:11:50,654
flash before Johnny's eyes.

277
00:11:52,696 --> 00:11:53,824
- [Voiceover] What a day,

278
00:11:53,824 --> 00:11:55,826
you never know who a fella will meet

279
00:11:55,826 --> 00:11:57,469
when he's looking for a helicopter,

280
00:11:57,469 --> 00:12:01,381
it's Barbara Ann Scott, the
World Champion Figure Skater.

281
00:12:01,381 --> 00:12:03,852
- [Joel] She's the Cher of her time.

282
00:12:03,852 --> 00:12:05,202
- [Crow] Jimminy, thinks Johnny,

283
00:12:05,202 --> 00:12:08,785
if only I could get a
ride in one of those!

284
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:12,971
- [Voiceover] Johnny does
find a real airplane,

285
00:12:12,971 --> 00:12:14,829
and gets his ride.

286
00:12:14,829 --> 00:12:16,117
- [Joel] Johnny thinks Amelia Earhart

287
00:12:16,117 --> 00:12:17,633
seems like a nice lady.

288
00:12:17,633 --> 00:12:19,043
- [Voiceover] They take
a spin on Lake Ontario

289
00:12:19,043 --> 00:12:21,889
to watch the start of the
international speedboat race.

290
00:12:21,889 --> 00:12:26,834
- [Joel] Whoa, Johnny realizes
he's in over his head.

291
00:12:26,834 --> 00:12:28,450
- [Crow] Johnny is irresponsibly
put into a dangerous

292
00:12:28,450 --> 00:12:30,852
speedboat without a life jacket.

293
00:12:30,852 --> 00:12:32,123
- [Joel] For the first
time in his young life,

294
00:12:32,123 --> 00:12:33,865
Johnny knows real fear.

295
00:12:33,865 --> 00:12:35,815
(screaming)

296
00:12:35,815 --> 00:12:39,482
Johnny's hydroplane
disintegrates on impact.

297
00:12:41,539 --> 00:12:43,658
- [Crow] Johnny's spirit
is completely broken.

298
00:12:43,658 --> 00:12:45,296
- [Voiceover] By now the
spring in Johnny's step

299
00:12:45,296 --> 00:12:47,729
is nearly gone, no lunch either.

300
00:12:47,729 --> 00:12:52,647
- [Joel] ♫ Way for sail,
he's going cheap. ♫

301
00:12:52,647 --> 00:12:54,302
- [Voiceover] Prime Ministers
are fine once in a while,

302
00:12:54,302 --> 00:12:56,356
but there's just so much a guy can take.

303
00:12:56,356 --> 00:13:00,028
- [Joel] Johnny realizes
what a lie his life has been.

304
00:13:00,028 --> 00:13:03,960
- [Voiceover] Right now,
Johnny wants his mother.

305
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:07,088
Perhaps Olsen and Johnson,
the Hellzapoppin' boys,

306
00:13:07,088 --> 00:13:08,657
can help cheer Johnny up.

307
00:13:08,657 --> 00:13:09,572
- [Crow] Yeah, but if
you've seen their act

308
00:13:09,572 --> 00:13:12,459
you know that's not likely.

309
00:13:12,459 --> 00:13:14,245
- [Voiceover] Johnny wants no part though.

310
00:13:14,245 --> 00:13:15,908
- [Joel] Johnny's got taste.

311
00:13:15,908 --> 00:13:17,148
- [Voiceover] But there's
tricks to every trade

312
00:13:17,148 --> 00:13:19,114
and the Hellzapoppin' Boys are tough,

313
00:13:19,114 --> 00:13:22,622
even a very tired and hungry
Johnny is able to laugh.

314
00:13:22,622 --> 00:13:25,955
- [Tom] Laugh, laugh, it's funny, laugh!

315
00:13:27,538 --> 00:13:29,636
- [Voiceover] Finally, a
friendly policeman takes Johnny

316
00:13:29,636 --> 00:13:33,136
to a building he hadn't planned on seeing.

317
00:13:34,686 --> 00:13:36,284
- [Tom] Let me out!

318
00:13:36,284 --> 00:13:37,534
Attica, Attica!

319
00:13:40,731 --> 00:13:42,822
- [Voiceover] There
are 350 acres of ground

320
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:45,569
in Exhibition Park and
Mom and Pop have covered

321
00:13:45,569 --> 00:13:48,605
every single acre looking for Johnny.

322
00:13:48,605 --> 00:13:50,401
- [Joel] Did I tell you to have this baby?

323
00:13:50,401 --> 00:13:51,506
- [Voiceover] They've looked everywhere.

324
00:13:51,506 --> 00:13:53,560
Everywhere but one place.

325
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,727
- [Crow] Their own hearts.

326
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:58,067
- [Voiceover] He's about so high.

327
00:13:58,067 --> 00:14:01,900
- [Joel] Well yes, there
was a Mr. Barty here.

328
00:14:04,591 --> 00:14:08,008
(cheering and whistling)

329
00:14:08,924 --> 00:14:11,997
- [Tom] Mommy had a little
vacation while you were lost.

330
00:14:11,997 --> 00:14:14,278
- [Joel] Yeah right,
play it up big in public.

331
00:14:14,278 --> 00:14:15,361
That's right.

332
00:14:17,586 --> 00:14:22,090
- [Tom] And I met Joe Lewis,
and the Prime Minister, and...

333
00:14:22,090 --> 00:14:25,358
- [Voiceover] Johnny fell
asleep on his father's shoulder.

334
00:14:25,358 --> 00:14:28,171
He had managed to stay awake
just long enough to see the

335
00:14:28,171 --> 00:14:30,211
beginning of the fireworks.

336
00:14:30,211 --> 00:14:31,287
- [Joel] At home.

337
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,791
- [Crow] Johnny's
parents blamed each other

338
00:14:32,791 --> 00:14:34,240
and never trusted again.

339
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,157
Good night.

340
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,084
- [Voiceover] Pleasant dreams, Johnny.

341
00:14:38,084 --> 00:14:40,167
- [Joel] So long, sucker.

342
00:14:41,061 --> 00:14:43,880
- [Crow] And let this
be a warning, to you!

343
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,963
(upbeat dance music)

344
00:14:49,788 --> 00:14:51,596
(base instrument music)

345
00:14:51,596 --> 00:14:53,948
Hey, there's a mingus among us.

346
00:14:53,948 --> 00:14:56,745
- [Tom] You know, I got the
nicest rebel set for my wedding.

347
00:14:56,745 --> 00:14:58,622
It's so nice.
- [Crow] Didja?

348
00:14:58,622 --> 00:15:00,872
Oh yeah, it's a reasonable.

349
00:15:02,082 --> 00:15:04,172
- [Crow] ♫ You say
petite, I'll say petite,

350
00:15:04,172 --> 00:15:06,115
♫ Let's call the whole thing off. ♫

351
00:15:06,115 --> 00:15:09,889
- [Joel] Man, I wish I could
afford a trap set, man.

352
00:15:09,889 --> 00:15:10,722
Man.

353
00:15:12,701 --> 00:15:14,226
- [Crow] Oh I never go
down to the village,

354
00:15:14,226 --> 00:15:15,725
they're too nutty down there.

355
00:15:15,725 --> 00:15:16,558
- [Crow] Oh yeah,
- [Tom] For sure.

356
00:15:16,558 --> 00:15:17,725
they're crazy.

357
00:15:19,802 --> 00:15:23,749
- [Joel] Looking very relaxed,
Adolf Hitler on vibes.

358
00:15:23,749 --> 00:15:26,416
(beatnik music)

359
00:15:28,019 --> 00:15:32,216
- [Tom] Cigar, cigarettes,
camu, startch, aunts,

360
00:15:32,216 --> 00:15:34,549
alienation, vikenstein, ohhh

361
00:15:35,789 --> 00:15:37,789
- [Joel] That was close.

362
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,524
(scatting)

363
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,713
Hey, it's Fisher and Statsky.

364
00:15:47,713 --> 00:15:51,260
- [Crow] ♫ One night in Bangkok
makes a strong man crumble ♫

365
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:56,171
- [Joel] Boy those rebels really
go through the Swiss Miss.

366
00:15:56,171 --> 00:15:57,737
- [Tom] You know, this is
the hippest Red Lobster

367
00:15:57,737 --> 00:15:58,820
I've been to.

368
00:16:00,063 --> 00:16:01,682
- [Joel] Watch it, here she comes again.

369
00:16:01,682 --> 00:16:03,849
(sighing)

370
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,250
(scatting)

371
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:13,726
Waitress, 'scuse me, can we get some...

372
00:16:13,726 --> 00:16:14,809
Oh forget it.

373
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:20,222
(scatting)

374
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:25,130
- For perfumes and prats
upon this beat still

375
00:16:26,027 --> 00:16:29,764
(Crow's fake snores drown out speaker)

376
00:16:29,764 --> 00:16:33,597
Through oceans and oceans
and legal commotion,

377
00:16:34,550 --> 00:16:37,800
good cologne on the beards of each man.

378
00:16:38,663 --> 00:16:39,895
- [Crow] Oh that's profound.

379
00:16:39,895 --> 00:16:40,728
Check please!

380
00:16:40,728 --> 00:16:42,221
- Oh King.

381
00:16:42,221 --> 00:16:43,054
- Hey!

382
00:16:43,929 --> 00:16:45,880
- [Joel] What do you want,
I'm a character actor.

383
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,613
- Good evening, Mr. T.

384
00:16:47,613 --> 00:16:48,446
- [Tom] Hi Mr. B.

385
00:16:48,446 --> 00:16:51,613
- Please, Sidney, it's Johnson's move.

386
00:16:53,005 --> 00:16:57,172
- [Crow] They're having a
goatee staring contest, well?

387
00:17:00,030 --> 00:17:02,240
- [Tom] Let's talk, we never talk.

388
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,443
- I'll have to take your Queen.

389
00:17:04,443 --> 00:17:07,110
- [Crow] Sorry about that chief.

390
00:17:08,316 --> 00:17:09,816
- Check, and mate.

391
00:17:10,975 --> 00:17:14,668
- [Joel] Hey, you knocked my block off.

392
00:17:14,668 --> 00:17:15,842
- You win Mr. Tucker.

393
00:17:15,842 --> 00:17:17,712
- [Joel] Mr. Drunker?
- 12 minutes.

394
00:17:17,712 --> 00:17:20,807
Perhaps you'll have better luck next time.

395
00:17:20,807 --> 00:17:24,009
- [Crow] Let's play Chutes
and Ladders next time.

396
00:17:24,009 --> 00:17:25,250
- [Joel] Milk money.

397
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:27,930
- Don't you ever lose one of those sets?

398
00:17:27,930 --> 00:17:30,101
- Rarely, if ever.
- [Joel] Thanks for asking...

399
00:17:30,101 --> 00:17:32,088
- Then you must be a
virtuoso, as they say.

400
00:17:32,088 --> 00:17:35,453
- Yes and no, I merely make
sure that my antagonists

401
00:17:35,453 --> 00:17:37,110
are bad chess players.

402
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:39,725
- [Joel] You're hard to talk to.

403
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:43,892
- Well watches, that comes
to an interesting $325.

404
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:46,520
- Oh, good hunting.

405
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,667
- [Crow] Boss, why are
you in your pajamas?

406
00:17:48,667 --> 00:17:49,856
- For the waitress you pinched, Sidney.

407
00:17:49,856 --> 00:17:51,927
- Oh Mr. T, what that's
how I express myself.

408
00:17:51,927 --> 00:17:53,253
- [Joel] Express this.

409
00:17:53,253 --> 00:17:55,925
- That might be quite true,
but this one is new here,

410
00:17:55,925 --> 00:17:57,567
I haven't pinched her myself yet.

411
00:17:57,567 --> 00:17:58,945
(booing)

412
00:17:58,945 --> 00:18:02,329
- I'm just sayin' Mr. T., good hunting.

413
00:18:02,329 --> 00:18:04,794
- Sidney, are you beat?

414
00:18:04,794 --> 00:18:07,895
- Oh sure man, cool, way
out and long gone, Daddy.

415
00:18:07,895 --> 00:18:10,382
- [Joel] Being sarcastic.

416
00:18:10,382 --> 00:18:12,747
- It just takes that you
want things, and it shows.

417
00:18:12,747 --> 00:18:14,909
- You want things yourself, Mr. T.;

418
00:18:14,909 --> 00:18:17,344
money, things, and eccetera.

419
00:18:17,344 --> 00:18:19,680
You own this joint and you work at it.

420
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,347
You even spotted them up.

421
00:18:21,347 --> 00:18:22,811
- [Joel] Don't ever say that.

422
00:18:22,811 --> 00:18:25,978
- When in Rome, Sidney, do the Romans.

423
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:30,026
Get these three gentlemen here
tonight after closing time.

424
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:32,383
- Then we're ready to move?

425
00:18:32,383 --> 00:18:33,313
- We are indeed.

426
00:18:33,313 --> 00:18:34,751
- [Joel] Tell 'em to bring boxes.

427
00:18:34,751 --> 00:18:36,801
- George Lelund, you kiddin'?

428
00:18:36,801 --> 00:18:38,179
- I never kid.

429
00:18:38,179 --> 00:18:40,345
- Lelund's nothin' but a wild, young punk.

430
00:18:40,345 --> 00:18:42,098
- [Crow] He's my wild, young punk.

431
00:18:42,098 --> 00:18:44,388
- He's also the best rifle shot I know.

432
00:18:44,388 --> 00:18:46,564
I believe it's the only thing
military school taught him.

433
00:18:46,564 --> 00:18:47,904
- [Joel] His name's Oswald.

434
00:18:47,904 --> 00:18:49,161
- Ray Miller?

435
00:18:49,161 --> 00:18:49,994
John Mapes, that ham roller?

436
00:18:49,994 --> 00:18:52,131
- [Joel] Come on, they're my friends.

437
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:54,631
- Si, Sidney, that ham roller.

438
00:18:57,125 --> 00:19:01,292
- [Crow] We have nothing
to fear, but fear itself.

439
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:08,435
I can't help it, I'm the Fonz, yeah?

440
00:19:10,165 --> 00:19:12,899
- [Tom] I hate character actors.

441
00:19:12,899 --> 00:19:14,935
- [John] I am a gentleman.

442
00:19:14,935 --> 00:19:16,689
- [Voiceover] That I'll try.

443
00:19:16,689 --> 00:19:18,655
- [Crow] Oh great, another
oily, unlikable character.

444
00:19:18,655 --> 00:19:20,250
- If you strike me again!

445
00:19:20,250 --> 00:19:23,086
- [Voiceover] So you may lose your arm.

446
00:19:23,086 --> 00:19:24,735
If you strike me you are

447
00:19:24,735 --> 00:19:25,568
no gentleman,
- [Joel] It's Miss Hathaway!

448
00:19:25,568 --> 00:19:28,651
And if no gentleman, why then no arm.

449
00:19:29,523 --> 00:19:32,801
- A herald cape, oh put me in thy books.

450
00:19:32,801 --> 00:19:34,384
What is your crest?

451
00:19:37,232 --> 00:19:38,589
A cockstone,
- [Man] Henry Miller.

452
00:19:38,589 --> 00:19:41,756
A cocktsone, a cockstone, a cockstone.

453
00:19:43,832 --> 00:19:44,879
- [Joel] Now wait a minute,

454
00:19:44,879 --> 00:19:46,001
it's a little late for acting lessons,

455
00:19:46,001 --> 00:19:47,981
they started filming already.

456
00:19:47,981 --> 00:19:49,141
- You're home kinda little late, Jeanne

457
00:19:49,141 --> 00:19:50,899
- [Crow] Yes Master.
- Last minute rush

458
00:19:50,899 --> 00:19:52,585
at the drive-in.

459
00:19:52,585 --> 00:19:54,387
One of the girls didn't show up.

460
00:19:54,387 --> 00:19:55,804
- [Crow] So, and?

461
00:19:56,725 --> 00:19:59,073
She's dressed like Jack Lalanne.

462
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:01,086
- What difference does it make anyway?

463
00:20:01,086 --> 00:20:03,498
- I just hate to see you
working so hard is all.

464
00:20:03,498 --> 00:20:06,149
- [Joel] Then get a job.

465
00:20:06,149 --> 00:20:07,759
- Then look the other way.

466
00:20:07,759 --> 00:20:08,926
- [Joel] Ouch.

467
00:20:11,186 --> 00:20:13,019
Murray, use a coaster.

468
00:20:15,067 --> 00:20:18,839
- You know, I can do
without cracks like that.

469
00:20:18,839 --> 00:20:19,839
- I'm sorry.

470
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,116
- I know it's rough on you honey,

471
00:20:22,116 --> 00:20:24,181
but once I get a break
- [Joel] A new shirt...

472
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:27,806
- Johnny, how much longer we
gonna wait for that break?

473
00:20:27,806 --> 00:20:29,411
- Well it could happen any day.

474
00:20:29,411 --> 00:20:33,294
- Well it hasn't happened for
the last year and a half now.

475
00:20:33,294 --> 00:20:34,925
(screaming in shock)

476
00:20:34,925 --> 00:20:36,814
- I'm an actor, I've gotta be seen around.

477
00:20:36,814 --> 00:20:39,584
- Where, in that beat coffee house?

478
00:20:39,584 --> 00:20:41,642
- What do you expect me to do?

479
00:20:41,642 --> 00:20:44,625
Make a fast 70, 80 bucks a week?

480
00:20:44,625 --> 00:20:48,735
- That 70, 80 a week, faster
than you're making now.

481
00:20:48,735 --> 00:20:50,531
- [Joel] Oh that hurts.

482
00:20:50,531 --> 00:20:52,122
- You used to have faith in me.

483
00:20:52,122 --> 00:20:53,486
- [Crow] Did I, when?

484
00:20:53,486 --> 00:20:56,510
- I used to have faith in
lots of things, Johnny.

485
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:58,010
Love conquers all.

486
00:20:59,301 --> 00:21:01,448
- [Tom] That is such a lie!

487
00:21:01,448 --> 00:21:05,567
- 20 room house in Beverly
Hills, three full swimming pools,

488
00:21:05,567 --> 00:21:06,774
- [Joel] You know, if you picked up

489
00:21:06,774 --> 00:21:09,470
a few more shifts you could move there.

490
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,252
- I don't believe in any of that anymore.

491
00:21:11,252 --> 00:21:13,097
- [Joel] Say hello to the folks, Susie.

492
00:21:13,097 --> 00:21:14,770
- And I don't think that
you really do either.

493
00:21:14,770 --> 00:21:18,310
- It's all going to
come true, it's got to.

494
00:21:18,310 --> 00:21:20,021
The law of averages.

495
00:21:20,021 --> 00:21:20,854
- [Joel] I'm average.

496
00:21:20,854 --> 00:21:21,687
I'll make it.

497
00:21:21,687 --> 00:21:23,524
- That law doesn't seem
to work for us, Johnny.

498
00:21:23,524 --> 00:21:25,578
- Hey come here.

499
00:21:25,578 --> 00:21:28,446
- [Tom] Ow, your implant inflated again.

500
00:21:28,446 --> 00:21:30,690
(telephone ringing)

501
00:21:30,690 --> 00:21:31,523
- I'll get it.

502
00:21:31,523 --> 00:21:33,773
- [Joel] Saved by the bell.

503
00:21:35,734 --> 00:21:38,554
- [Tom] Go ahead, answer
the phone, Montgomery Clift.

504
00:21:38,554 --> 00:21:42,600
- [Joel] Oh, this must be
that guy from pomade calling.

505
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:43,433
- Hello?

506
00:21:44,669 --> 00:21:45,752
Sidney, yeah?

507
00:21:47,447 --> 00:21:48,308
Bernie!

508
00:21:48,308 --> 00:21:49,382
- [Joel] How's Bridget?

509
00:21:49,382 --> 00:21:51,294
- Hey, it's about time you gave me a call.

510
00:21:51,294 --> 00:21:53,396
- [Crow] Fat brown suit,
eight bucks a week?

511
00:21:53,396 --> 00:21:55,390
- The producer wants to meet me?

512
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:56,223
Tonight?

513
00:21:58,830 --> 00:22:00,911
I'll be over like a guided missile.

514
00:22:00,911 --> 00:22:02,930
- [Joel] Only bigger and dumber.

515
00:22:02,930 --> 00:22:05,284
- Baby, this might be it.

516
00:22:05,284 --> 00:22:06,746
- Who was it?

517
00:22:06,746 --> 00:22:08,812
- Bernie my agent,
- [Crow] Bernstein?

518
00:22:08,812 --> 00:22:10,736
Set up a meeting for me
tonight at 12 o'clock,

519
00:22:10,736 --> 00:22:12,968
with a Broadway producer.

520
00:22:12,968 --> 00:22:14,570
- [Tom] Show called, Moose Murders.

521
00:22:14,570 --> 00:22:16,005
- That late at night?

522
00:22:16,005 --> 00:22:18,380
- Honey, you know show business?

523
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:20,385
Why if a guy wants to meet me at midnight,

524
00:22:20,385 --> 00:22:22,354
so I'll meet the guy at midnight.

525
00:22:22,354 --> 00:22:24,286
Oh come on, how 'bout dinner, huh?

526
00:22:24,286 --> 00:22:25,406
- [Joel] Ring baloney?

527
00:22:25,406 --> 00:22:29,372
- You know the old saying, a
hungry actor never gets a job.

528
00:22:29,372 --> 00:22:32,522
- [Crow] I've never heard that.

529
00:22:32,522 --> 00:22:35,108
- [Joel] She's not buying it.

530
00:22:35,108 --> 00:22:36,396
- [Crow] Last night it was Joe Papp,

531
00:22:36,396 --> 00:22:38,917
then it was Herald Prince,
I'm sick of it, sick.

532
00:22:38,917 --> 00:22:40,761
- Well, back to junior jumble.

533
00:22:40,761 --> 00:22:42,183
Here I go.

534
00:22:42,183 --> 00:22:44,433
- [Crow] Act with Rosemary.

535
00:22:48,602 --> 00:22:51,519
(train on a track)

536
00:22:52,602 --> 00:22:55,269
(door shutting)

537
00:23:02,377 --> 00:23:04,403
- It came, it came, it came.

538
00:23:04,403 --> 00:23:06,012
You guys, Joel,

539
00:23:06,012 --> 00:23:08,534
open it up.
- [Joel] Hey Crow,

540
00:23:08,534 --> 00:23:09,617
what is this?

541
00:23:10,635 --> 00:23:13,601
- Well you see, four to six
weeks ago I ordered a series

542
00:23:13,601 --> 00:23:18,169
of acting lessons on records
from the So You Want to Act,

543
00:23:18,169 --> 00:23:20,687
Institute of Acting,
just like in the movie.

544
00:23:20,687 --> 00:23:22,173
- Oh lucky, hey did you order those

545
00:23:22,173 --> 00:23:24,259
from those Sally Struthers
commercials where she goes,

546
00:23:24,259 --> 00:23:26,482
"Do you wanna make more money?

547
00:23:26,482 --> 00:23:28,523
Sure we all do."

548
00:23:28,523 --> 00:23:29,356
- No.

549
00:23:29,356 --> 00:23:32,600
- It says, costarring
with Scott Baio, you.

550
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:37,428
Okay lets see here, we've got
scenes from Charles in Charge,

551
00:23:37,428 --> 00:23:39,345
scenes from Happy Days,

552
00:23:40,732 --> 00:23:43,455
we got scenes from Lansky's Beauties,

553
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:45,510
scenes from Who's Watchin' the Kids,

554
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:47,676
and scenes from Joanie Loves Chachi.

555
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:49,260
- Yes!

556
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:51,666
I decided against the deluxe
edition, which included scenes

557
00:23:51,666 --> 00:23:53,959
from his movies, Zapped, Bugsy Malone,

558
00:23:53,959 --> 00:23:56,032
of course you knew that, and
The Boy that Drank too Much.

559
00:23:56,032 --> 00:23:57,653
I just didn't think I was ready, and

560
00:23:57,653 --> 00:24:00,766
I thought it would give me
something to work towards.

561
00:24:00,766 --> 00:24:04,932
Okay, it says here for
this scene, I'm Joanie.

562
00:24:04,932 --> 00:24:06,017
- Hey Joanie.

563
00:24:06,017 --> 00:24:07,184
- Hey Chachie.

564
00:24:08,469 --> 00:24:09,729
Uhh, no, no, no, no.

565
00:24:09,729 --> 00:24:12,459
That's not right, I'm sorry,

566
00:24:12,459 --> 00:24:13,292
can we take it from the top everyone?

567
00:24:13,292 --> 00:24:14,125
Please.

568
00:24:14,125 --> 00:24:15,315
Thank you.

569
00:24:15,315 --> 00:24:16,659
- [Tom] Hey Joanie.

570
00:24:16,659 --> 00:24:17,698
- Hey Chachie.

571
00:24:17,698 --> 00:24:18,698
Hey Chachie.

572
00:24:20,318 --> 00:24:23,815
No, excuse me but, what
exactly is the subject here?

573
00:24:23,815 --> 00:24:28,381
Is hey combative, or a derivative,
or just conversational?

574
00:24:28,381 --> 00:24:31,821
- Well it sounds like an
affectionate acknowledgement to me.

575
00:24:31,821 --> 00:24:34,055
- Well remember Crow, at this
point in Joanie and Chachie's

576
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:36,509
relationship they're newlyweds
and they have this entire

577
00:24:36,509 --> 00:24:38,750
history together from
their years on Happy Days,

578
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:40,747
so there's also that dynamic.

579
00:24:40,747 --> 00:24:42,773
And they're struggling with Chachie's

580
00:24:42,773 --> 00:24:44,325
fledgling singing career.

581
00:24:44,325 --> 00:24:46,440
- True, and Joanie is also
trying to cope with the fact

582
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:49,218
that all their female friends
see her husband, Chachie,

583
00:24:49,218 --> 00:24:50,810
as a hunky heart throb.

584
00:24:50,810 --> 00:24:51,810
- Precisely.

585
00:24:52,860 --> 00:24:54,499
- Hey Chachie.

586
00:24:54,499 --> 00:24:56,120
- Crow you got it.

587
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:56,953
- Really?

588
00:24:56,953 --> 00:24:58,229
- Yeah.
- [Crow] Think so?

589
00:24:58,229 --> 00:25:00,287
- Yeah, we'll be right back.

590
00:25:00,287 --> 00:25:02,806
- Yeah, guys I'm gonna need a
big hug after rehearsal today.

591
00:25:02,806 --> 00:25:04,389
- You are so tense.

592
00:25:06,532 --> 00:25:09,615
(upbeat dance music)

593
00:25:15,151 --> 00:25:16,979
- [Tom] Hey look, you know who that is?

594
00:25:16,979 --> 00:25:17,996
- [Crow] No.
- [Tom] I'll give you a hint,

595
00:25:17,996 --> 00:25:19,398
♫ I sing whenever I sing whenever I sing ♫

596
00:25:19,398 --> 00:25:20,433
- [Crow] Oh no.

597
00:25:20,433 --> 00:25:21,433
- [Tom] Yup.

598
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:26,980
- [Joel] Hey, the cops ate my chiclets.

599
00:25:28,522 --> 00:25:29,935
Hey, how come I don't even know you,

600
00:25:29,935 --> 00:25:33,644
and you keep bailing me out, what gives?

601
00:25:33,644 --> 00:25:35,010
- [Crow] Hey Vern!

602
00:25:35,010 --> 00:25:39,103
- [Joel] Ernest does
a nickel up in Attica.

603
00:25:39,103 --> 00:25:40,475
- How'd you get into the act?

604
00:25:40,475 --> 00:25:41,617
- [Joel] I replaced Gummo.

605
00:25:41,617 --> 00:25:44,177
- [Tom] I'm your guardian angel.

606
00:25:44,177 --> 00:25:46,440
- Mr. Tucker wants to see
you tonight after closing.

607
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,273
- [Crow] Strike the set.

608
00:25:47,273 --> 00:25:48,600
- What for?

609
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:51,362
Doesn't he know that my
mother won't gimme a dime.

610
00:25:51,362 --> 00:25:53,489
Unless I straighten up and
go live with her on that

611
00:25:53,489 --> 00:25:55,576
lousy ranch her husband gave her.

612
00:25:55,576 --> 00:25:58,046
- Mr. T. Just wants to make
you a business proposition.

613
00:25:58,046 --> 00:25:59,681
- Me?

614
00:25:59,681 --> 00:26:01,213
That's a laugh.

615
00:26:01,213 --> 00:26:02,258
(fake laughter from audience)

616
00:26:02,258 --> 00:26:06,215
- Mr. Tucker don't appreciate
laughing, so you just beat it.

617
00:26:06,215 --> 00:26:08,026
- Hey Leland!

618
00:26:08,026 --> 00:26:10,571
- [Joel] Love that shot!

619
00:26:10,571 --> 00:26:12,609
(beatnik music)

620
00:26:12,609 --> 00:26:13,716
Wait, what's his deal?

621
00:26:13,716 --> 00:26:15,883
- [Crow] Oh, it's a woman.

622
00:26:17,565 --> 00:26:20,086
You know guys, if this is
what being beat was all about

623
00:26:20,086 --> 00:26:24,198
I'd rather be a shallow
post-boomer, like you.

624
00:26:24,198 --> 00:26:25,281
- [Joel] Hey.

625
00:26:27,705 --> 00:26:29,870
- [Crow] Oh, it's a Jules Feiffer cartoon.

626
00:26:29,870 --> 00:26:32,370
(flute music)

627
00:26:35,321 --> 00:26:37,738
- [Joel] Hey, it's Olive Oil.

628
00:26:38,984 --> 00:26:40,567
- [Crow] Oh Popeye.

629
00:26:42,292 --> 00:26:46,459
- [Joel] Maybe we shouldn't
have gotten rid of the T.V.?

630
00:26:48,254 --> 00:26:51,587
Oh I get it, it's a Sadie Hawkins Dance.

631
00:26:52,521 --> 00:26:54,158
- [Crow] There's a painting
of Marty Allen back there.

632
00:26:54,158 --> 00:26:55,158
Hello there.

633
00:26:58,562 --> 00:27:02,729
- [Joel] Yeah, I need liquor
to deal with this weird action.

634
00:27:03,825 --> 00:27:05,839
- [Tom] Kinda like beatnik twister, huh?

635
00:27:05,839 --> 00:27:06,914
- [Joel] Twisted Sister.

636
00:27:06,914 --> 00:27:09,017
- [Crow] Forbidden dance of Laura Petrie.

637
00:27:09,017 --> 00:27:13,045
- [Joel] The more I drink,
the more talented you become.

638
00:27:13,045 --> 00:27:14,648
- [Tom] They remind me of Fred and Ginger.

639
00:27:14,648 --> 00:27:16,976
- [Crow] Yeah, Fred
Travalena and Ginger Baker.

640
00:27:16,976 --> 00:27:18,059
- [Tom] Zing!

641
00:27:21,615 --> 00:27:23,039
- [Crow] Look at the pie on him.

642
00:27:23,039 --> 00:27:24,650
- [Joel] Oh my God.

643
00:27:24,650 --> 00:27:28,194
I told you kids, no
parties while I'm gone!

644
00:27:28,194 --> 00:27:32,361
- [Crow] I've come to
look at the apartment.

645
00:27:32,361 --> 00:27:35,424
- You're pretty far out I'd say.

646
00:27:35,424 --> 00:27:37,685
- Far out and floating.

647
00:27:37,685 --> 00:27:41,079
I just received the seventh
rejection, and I'm on one now.

648
00:27:41,079 --> 00:27:42,070
- Congratulations.

649
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:43,607
- [Joel] No see that means it didn't sell.

650
00:27:43,607 --> 00:27:45,170
It's a bad thing.

651
00:27:45,170 --> 00:27:47,011
- You and me gotta make some conversation

652
00:27:47,011 --> 00:27:49,594
where it's a little more quiet.

653
00:27:55,097 --> 00:27:55,930
- [Joel] You know, all these people

654
00:27:55,930 --> 00:27:58,288
are in middle management now.

655
00:27:58,288 --> 00:28:00,846
- You know what they say about my book?

656
00:28:00,846 --> 00:28:02,429
- [Crow] It sucked?

657
00:28:04,037 --> 00:28:05,445
- They say it stinks.

658
00:28:05,445 --> 00:28:06,278
- [Joel] Smell it, see if you agree.

659
00:28:06,278 --> 00:28:09,075
- You know, the funny part
about it is that they're right.

660
00:28:09,075 --> 00:28:11,151
- What do you care what they think?

661
00:28:11,151 --> 00:28:15,223
- A year of my life went
into that stinkin' book.

662
00:28:15,223 --> 00:28:17,343
- Writin' books is for eggheads.

663
00:28:17,343 --> 00:28:19,306
- Mr. T's got a better idea.

664
00:28:19,306 --> 00:28:20,418
- T?

665
00:28:20,418 --> 00:28:21,442
Tucker.

666
00:28:21,442 --> 00:28:22,715
- The same.

667
00:28:22,715 --> 00:28:25,757
Sober up and be at the coffee
house after closing tonight.

668
00:28:25,757 --> 00:28:28,340
- [Joel] My Three Sons go beat.

669
00:28:30,539 --> 00:28:32,502
- There's no place else I got to go.

670
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:35,752
- [Crow] Don't get no better than this.

671
00:28:38,155 --> 00:28:40,121
- [Joel] Theo Bikel?

672
00:28:40,121 --> 00:28:42,121
This must be 200 Motels.

673
00:28:43,997 --> 00:28:46,070
- [Tom] Wonder how I can
make my life more depressing?

674
00:28:46,070 --> 00:28:47,320
Try this place.

675
00:28:50,404 --> 00:28:51,455
- [Crow] It's the devil's workshop.

676
00:28:51,455 --> 00:28:53,538
- [Tom] Hey, there he is.

677
00:28:55,213 --> 00:28:58,306
- [Joel] A character
actor to see you, sir.

678
00:28:58,306 --> 00:28:59,746
- Grab a chair, it's on the house.

679
00:28:59,746 --> 00:29:00,656
- Thanks.

680
00:29:00,656 --> 00:29:02,284
- You cats more or less acquainted?

681
00:29:02,284 --> 00:29:03,117
- Yeah.

682
00:29:03,982 --> 00:29:05,252
- Then we can start you off from scratch.

683
00:29:05,252 --> 00:29:07,336
- [Crow] Can I start you
off with some appetizers?

684
00:29:07,336 --> 00:29:10,119
- Too bad we ain't got no
floor show for you gents,

685
00:29:10,119 --> 00:29:12,614
but once Mr. T goes into his
filibuster you ain't gonna

686
00:29:12,614 --> 00:29:14,995
miss the dancin' girls at all.

687
00:29:14,995 --> 00:29:16,486
- [Crow] Shut up.
- [Joel] Shut up.

688
00:29:16,486 --> 00:29:18,148
- Not that we ever get much romantics

689
00:29:18,148 --> 00:29:20,033
in these here surroundings.

690
00:29:20,033 --> 00:29:21,220
- Sidney I don't dig you.

691
00:29:21,220 --> 00:29:23,889
All this chopper music but no tune.

692
00:29:23,889 --> 00:29:25,992
- You know what the trouble
with you beat guys is?

693
00:29:25,992 --> 00:29:27,449
- [Joel] You're so '50s.

694
00:29:27,449 --> 00:29:29,156
- Who's you in likeness?

695
00:29:29,156 --> 00:29:31,629
- You don't talk English very good.

696
00:29:31,629 --> 00:29:33,246
- Come on, Tucker didn't get us over here

697
00:29:33,246 --> 00:29:34,508
to improve our speech.

698
00:29:34,508 --> 00:29:35,609
- [Tom] Ernest Hemingway?

699
00:29:35,609 --> 00:29:39,206
- Not your speech, gentlemen,
but perhaps your finances.

700
00:29:39,206 --> 00:29:40,460
- [Tom] Pyramid Game?

701
00:29:40,460 --> 00:29:43,156
- The man is talking about Brent?

702
00:29:43,156 --> 00:29:45,507
- The man is talking about money.

703
00:29:45,507 --> 00:29:47,281
- [Crow] Get your paws off
me you damn, dirty beat!

704
00:29:47,281 --> 00:29:49,363
- You gentlemen have been
among my steadiest customers.

705
00:29:49,363 --> 00:29:51,520
I've had the opportunity
of studying you closely.

706
00:29:51,520 --> 00:29:54,750
- You're writing the great American novel?

707
00:29:54,750 --> 00:29:58,917
- [Joel] No, I'm doing a
Northern Exposure spec script.

708
00:30:00,514 --> 00:30:02,625
- Nor am I casting a play,

709
00:30:02,625 --> 00:30:06,206
nor attempting to furnish
psychological guidance

710
00:30:06,206 --> 00:30:08,427
to a poor little rich boy.

711
00:30:08,427 --> 00:30:09,430
- Alright, alright.

712
00:30:09,430 --> 00:30:11,075
You've told us what you're not doing,

713
00:30:11,075 --> 00:30:13,561
now would you mind telling
us what you are doing?

714
00:30:13,561 --> 00:30:14,501
- Not at all.

715
00:30:14,501 --> 00:30:16,159
- [Joel] I'm reading
for Mel Brooks tomorrow.

716
00:30:16,159 --> 00:30:18,549
- I'm preparing, with your cooperation,

717
00:30:18,549 --> 00:30:21,070
to steal a million dollars.

718
00:30:21,070 --> 00:30:22,820
- [Joel] Feel eleven.

719
00:30:23,744 --> 00:30:25,226
- You say steal?

720
00:30:25,226 --> 00:30:27,663
- Do you know anyone who's
giving away a million dollars?

721
00:30:27,663 --> 00:30:28,688
- [Tom] Ed McMahon?

722
00:30:28,688 --> 00:30:30,110
- Except Uncle Sam, of course.

723
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:31,596
- [Crow] I don't get it.

724
00:30:31,596 --> 00:30:35,304
- You're talkin' about some sort of crime?

725
00:30:35,304 --> 00:30:37,381
- What's in a name?

726
00:30:37,381 --> 00:30:40,109
A writer of some ability once remarked,

727
00:30:40,109 --> 00:30:44,297
"A rose by any other name,
would still have thornes."

728
00:30:44,297 --> 00:30:45,664
- [Tom] I think you're misquoting.

729
00:30:45,664 --> 00:30:47,914
- [Mr. T] Certainly, Karen?

730
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:50,309
- [Joel] Did you call me Karen?

731
00:30:50,309 --> 00:30:52,421
- What I wanna know is, why'd you pick us?

732
00:30:52,421 --> 00:30:53,776
I mean us three.

733
00:30:53,776 --> 00:30:55,347
- [Crow] I Saw your audition tape.

734
00:30:55,347 --> 00:30:57,984
- Because none of you are
beat, you're merely beaten.

735
00:30:57,984 --> 00:31:00,951
You're not detached, you're unemployed.

736
00:31:00,951 --> 00:31:05,723
You're not dispassionate,
you're afraid, scared.

737
00:31:05,723 --> 00:31:08,116
- [Joel] Can I still get
an omelette or something?

738
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:11,751
- [Tom] She just put her brain in.

739
00:31:11,751 --> 00:31:13,173
What do I look like, a waitress?

740
00:31:13,173 --> 00:31:14,523
Oh wait, I am.

741
00:31:14,523 --> 00:31:16,676
- In exchange for a
few days of your lives,

742
00:31:16,676 --> 00:31:20,583
I'm offering each one of you $200,000.

743
00:31:20,583 --> 00:31:22,000
- [Crow] Okay, three.

744
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:24,850
- Money enough for you
to forget you can't act.

745
00:31:24,850 --> 00:31:27,604
- [Joel] Hey, you're
in this film, too, bud.

746
00:31:27,604 --> 00:31:30,771
- Perhaps start reading good ones.

747
00:31:30,771 --> 00:31:33,267
For you to cut lose from your
lovely and wandering mother,

748
00:31:33,267 --> 00:31:36,524
so that you may go to
hell in your own way.

749
00:31:36,524 --> 00:31:40,153
- [Joel] That's kind of a
back handed compliment, huh?

750
00:31:40,153 --> 00:31:44,320
- [Crow] Thanks for those
quick character sketches, boss.

751
00:31:45,757 --> 00:31:47,918
- My plan is based on
the interesting fact that

752
00:31:47,918 --> 00:31:51,594
if you take a train from
Los Angeles to New York,

753
00:31:51,594 --> 00:31:53,993
there's a four hour stop over in Chicago.

754
00:31:53,993 --> 00:31:55,706
- [Joel] It's the SAT caber.

755
00:31:55,706 --> 00:31:56,794
- What's so interesting about

756
00:31:56,794 --> 00:31:58,789
Chicago?
- [Tom] My kind of town.

757
00:31:58,789 --> 00:32:01,612
- Any town where you steal a
million dollars is interesting.

758
00:32:01,612 --> 00:32:03,261
Before I go into details...

759
00:32:03,261 --> 00:32:04,696
- [Crow] Let's have a song!

760
00:32:04,696 --> 00:32:07,134
I wanna press upon you that
no one can change their mind.

761
00:32:07,134 --> 00:32:09,259
No one.
- [Joel] Okay, you can.

762
00:32:09,259 --> 00:32:12,105
Notice I didn't put that as a question,

763
00:32:12,105 --> 00:32:15,887
for the simple reason that
I can buy any of your debts

764
00:32:15,887 --> 00:32:17,940
for x dollars.

765
00:32:17,940 --> 00:32:18,977
- [Tom] From Sharper Image.

766
00:32:18,977 --> 00:32:22,358
- And x dollars can make
any of you x permanently.

767
00:32:22,358 --> 00:32:24,751
- [Joel] And that's exactly what I mean.

768
00:32:24,751 --> 00:32:26,894
- [Crow] Okay, who ordered the Special X?

769
00:32:26,894 --> 00:32:29,301
- [Tom] I had the Dos X's.

770
00:32:29,301 --> 00:32:30,883
- This isn't what I had in mind.

771
00:32:30,883 --> 00:32:32,172
- I don't have a liquor license and

772
00:32:32,172 --> 00:32:35,150
I don't believe in breaking small laws.

773
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:38,233
- [Tom] There are no small
laws, just small criminals.

774
00:32:38,233 --> 00:32:39,483
- As per usual.

775
00:32:41,176 --> 00:32:44,338
- Tomorrow you will get some
presentable clothes, and

776
00:32:44,338 --> 00:32:45,507
perhaps a shave.

777
00:32:45,507 --> 00:32:47,157
- [Joe] And a haircut two bits.

778
00:32:47,157 --> 00:32:49,914
- You have plenty enough to travel.

779
00:32:49,914 --> 00:32:51,965
Now the details of your exact duties,

780
00:32:51,965 --> 00:32:54,080
our meeting place in Chicago and so forth,

781
00:32:54,080 --> 00:32:55,679
you'll get from Sidney.

782
00:32:55,679 --> 00:32:57,716
Your train tickets will be picked up here

783
00:32:57,716 --> 00:32:59,722
tomorrow night at 8:30.

784
00:32:59,722 --> 00:33:01,389
- [Crow] Okay, nine.

785
00:33:02,246 --> 00:33:04,132
- Congratulations on
your association with me

786
00:33:04,132 --> 00:33:05,982
on this magnificent undertaking.

787
00:33:05,982 --> 00:33:06,951
- [Joel] Enjoy your sodas.

788
00:33:06,951 --> 00:33:09,052
- It'll not only be financially rewarding,

789
00:33:09,052 --> 00:33:11,820
but it might also bring us fame.

790
00:33:11,820 --> 00:33:13,487
Anonymous of course.

791
00:33:15,221 --> 00:33:18,020
Now for the details of the master plan.

792
00:33:18,020 --> 00:33:20,325
- [Joel] First, you'll take
this Precious Moment's figure

793
00:33:20,325 --> 00:33:24,384
and set it next to a clock
and an ashtray, then...

794
00:33:24,384 --> 00:33:28,551
- [Tom] ♫ One less bell to
answer, one less egg to fry ♫

795
00:33:35,083 --> 00:33:38,094
- [Crow] Honey, Kazan wants
me for On the Waterfront Two,

796
00:33:38,094 --> 00:33:41,277
Electric Booblaloo.
- [Jeanne] Johnny?

797
00:33:41,277 --> 00:33:44,610
- [Joel] Are you in another movie, dear?

798
00:33:45,563 --> 00:33:47,614
- It's almost 4 o'clock.

799
00:33:47,614 --> 00:33:48,447
- I know.

800
00:33:49,487 --> 00:33:51,526
The producer was the windy type.

801
00:33:51,526 --> 00:33:52,527
- [Tom] Kind of an actor vampire type,

802
00:33:52,527 --> 00:33:54,560
can't see his ego in the mirror.

803
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:55,560
- Who is he?

804
00:33:56,592 --> 00:33:58,221
- [Crow] Uhh, Joe, uhh David.

805
00:33:58,221 --> 00:34:01,591
- Well, he probably has a name.

806
00:34:01,591 --> 00:34:02,730
- Sal Houston

807
00:34:02,730 --> 00:34:03,964
- [Joel] Big Jew from Texas.

808
00:34:03,964 --> 00:34:06,847
- Never heard of him, Broadway?

809
00:34:06,847 --> 00:34:11,800
- Really he's a show backer,
he has a civic of investors.

810
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:14,890
He said I was just right for the part.

811
00:34:14,890 --> 00:34:17,175
- [Joel] The Jethro Bodine Story?

812
00:34:17,175 --> 00:34:19,287
- Oh Johnny, you're not kidding!

813
00:34:19,287 --> 00:34:21,543
- At 4 o' clock in the morning I'm not.

814
00:34:21,543 --> 00:34:22,876
Why the devil can't a woman ever

815
00:34:22,876 --> 00:34:26,120
learn a simple way of
squeezing a tube of toothpaste?

816
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:28,564
- Well then you did get it, huh?

817
00:34:28,564 --> 00:34:31,647
(upbeat dance music)

818
00:34:36,082 --> 00:34:40,082
- [Tom] Charles Foster
Kent and Martha Mitchell.

819
00:34:42,491 --> 00:34:44,658
(yelling)

820
00:34:47,134 --> 00:34:50,395
- [Joel] People try to put us down.

821
00:34:50,395 --> 00:34:52,787
- [Crow] The Lockhorn's go slumming.

822
00:34:52,787 --> 00:34:55,397
- You behave yourself, you
want them to accept you.

823
00:34:55,397 --> 00:34:56,282
- Accept me?

824
00:34:56,282 --> 00:34:57,691
That's not the idea.

825
00:34:57,691 --> 00:34:59,101
Will I accept them?

826
00:34:59,101 --> 00:35:00,268
- Bertha Luna.

827
00:35:01,955 --> 00:35:03,629
- What's that?

828
00:35:03,629 --> 00:35:04,629
Unmask, sir.

829
00:35:05,671 --> 00:35:10,570
- Shh, that's King and
David, our poetry laureate.

830
00:35:10,570 --> 00:35:13,456
- Oh I see, I guess he yodels, too.

831
00:35:13,456 --> 00:35:14,289
- Oh Russ.

832
00:35:16,523 --> 00:35:17,633
- Tourists.

833
00:35:17,633 --> 00:35:20,560
- [Tom] Old one eye is back.

834
00:35:20,560 --> 00:35:23,469
- From nothingness to nothingness.

835
00:35:23,469 --> 00:35:26,488
- [Joel] He's reading the menu.

836
00:35:26,488 --> 00:35:28,555
- [Tom] Nice one.

837
00:35:28,555 --> 00:35:29,994
- That's us goin' a fools' errand

838
00:35:29,994 --> 00:35:32,072
before they throw a butterfly net over us.

839
00:35:32,072 --> 00:35:35,210
- [Crow] Hey man, that's beautiful.

840
00:35:35,210 --> 00:35:36,713
- I've got my eye on you.

841
00:35:36,713 --> 00:35:38,546
- [Tom] My hungry eye.

842
00:35:39,651 --> 00:35:41,111
- And vice versa.

843
00:35:41,111 --> 00:35:44,549
- And that includes your language.

844
00:35:44,549 --> 00:35:46,220
- [Joel] Wait, it doesn't
say that in the script.

845
00:35:46,220 --> 00:35:47,951
Where did that all come from?

846
00:35:47,951 --> 00:35:51,305
- A sad train, are the five senses.

847
00:35:51,305 --> 00:35:52,909
- [Crow] I always get
the skillet scramble.

848
00:35:52,909 --> 00:35:56,018
- At least we won't have to
listen to that stuff anymore.

849
00:35:56,018 --> 00:35:58,526
- I happen to like it.

850
00:35:58,526 --> 00:36:01,091
- Well I like ole' Betsy better.

851
00:36:01,091 --> 00:36:03,294
- That rifle make you
feel anymore like a man?

852
00:36:03,294 --> 00:36:05,877
- Smell nostrils, hear old ears

853
00:36:07,826 --> 00:36:10,176
- Bravo old majesty.

854
00:36:10,176 --> 00:36:12,874
- Thank you, old squid.

855
00:36:12,874 --> 00:36:13,957
- [Crow] Hey, that'd make a great term

856
00:36:13,957 --> 00:36:15,440
for someone who's not very hip.

857
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:16,623
- [Joel] Yes it would.

858
00:36:16,623 --> 00:36:19,123
- [Tom] Thank you, Mr. Cooper.

859
00:36:21,605 --> 00:36:24,078
I think he's doin', Crap's Last Eight.

860
00:36:24,078 --> 00:36:27,105
- A hat box, it has no content.

861
00:36:27,105 --> 00:36:28,689
- [Crow] Much like this film.

862
00:36:28,689 --> 00:36:30,725
- A brain is missing.

863
00:36:30,725 --> 00:36:33,146
- It's been missing all night!

864
00:36:33,146 --> 00:36:35,774
- [Joel] Do you mind if
we dance with your date?

865
00:36:35,774 --> 00:36:37,691
- Gentlemen, gentlemen.

866
00:36:38,551 --> 00:36:40,865
- [Joel] Could we get
our order to go, please.

867
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:42,819
- King, we enjoyed it.

868
00:36:42,819 --> 00:36:43,893
Truly we did.

869
00:36:43,893 --> 00:36:47,711
- [Crow] My husband's very hip at home.

870
00:36:47,711 --> 00:36:48,878
- I am bugged.

871
00:36:50,419 --> 00:36:53,152
- [Joel] God of Facial Hair!

872
00:36:53,152 --> 00:36:55,123
(cheering and whistling)

873
00:36:55,123 --> 00:36:56,416
- Irwin Corey, everyone.

874
00:36:56,416 --> 00:36:57,903
Irwin Corey.

875
00:36:57,903 --> 00:36:59,153
- I'm so sorry.

876
00:37:00,429 --> 00:37:01,400
- [Tom] What're you tellin' me for,

877
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:03,767
I'm Lyle Waggoner, aren't I?

878
00:37:03,767 --> 00:37:04,934
No, maybe not.

879
00:37:07,802 --> 00:37:09,930
- Well, the noble thespian has arrived.

880
00:37:09,930 --> 00:37:11,923
- [Joel] Hey, I'm as
hetero as the next guy.

881
00:37:11,923 --> 00:37:12,902
- You got the tickets?

882
00:37:12,902 --> 00:37:14,482
- No but they're here.

883
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:16,327
Tucker left 'em with Miss I.Q.

884
00:37:16,327 --> 00:37:18,088
before her took off for
Chicago with Sidney.

885
00:37:18,088 --> 00:37:19,921
- Well, what happened?

886
00:37:20,771 --> 00:37:23,498
- She won't part with them
'til the stroke of 8:30.

887
00:37:23,498 --> 00:37:25,373
She takes Tucker's word rather literally.

888
00:37:25,373 --> 00:37:27,776
(audience making siren sounds)

889
00:37:27,776 --> 00:37:30,634
- Did I see you adult--adulterating,

890
00:37:30,634 --> 00:37:32,158
oh spiking that coke?
- [Joel] Cut!

891
00:37:32,158 --> 00:37:33,325
It's medicine.

892
00:37:34,371 --> 00:37:36,664
Four out of five New York
doctors recommend it.

893
00:37:36,664 --> 00:37:38,420
- Oh really?

894
00:37:38,420 --> 00:37:40,589
- [Crow] Wow, what a comeback.

895
00:37:40,589 --> 00:37:42,034
- Yes?

896
00:37:42,034 --> 00:37:44,061
- What about the tickets?

897
00:37:44,061 --> 00:37:45,895
- You'll get them at 8:30.

898
00:37:45,895 --> 00:37:47,070
- But it is 8:30.

899
00:37:47,070 --> 00:37:48,329
- [Tom] Somewhere in the world.

900
00:37:48,329 --> 00:37:50,329
- It is 8:10, precisely.

901
00:37:51,395 --> 00:37:52,464
- Karen,
- [Joel] I'll have the

902
00:37:52,464 --> 00:37:53,750
chicken wings.

903
00:37:53,750 --> 00:37:55,055
- Yes, John?

904
00:37:55,055 --> 00:37:58,135
- Where'd you get that pretty watch?

905
00:37:58,135 --> 00:38:02,878
- Dear Sidney sold it to me,
and at a great personal loss.

906
00:38:02,878 --> 00:38:03,795
- I'll bet.

907
00:38:04,933 --> 00:38:06,087
- [Crow] Ow!

908
00:38:06,087 --> 00:38:07,266
- Well, it's not working.

909
00:38:07,266 --> 00:38:08,341
- Huh?

910
00:38:08,341 --> 00:38:09,452
- [Tom] My wrist?

911
00:38:09,452 --> 00:38:11,925
It still works, see?

912
00:38:11,925 --> 00:38:13,116
(knocking)

913
00:38:13,116 --> 00:38:14,200
Come in?

914
00:38:14,200 --> 00:38:16,377
No wonder it's been 8:10 for three days.

915
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:20,795
- I'll never trust that
Sidney again, that H-E-A-L.

916
00:38:20,795 --> 00:38:22,778
- [Tom] She's Danielle Quayle.

917
00:38:22,778 --> 00:38:24,950
- Now would you mind
giving us the tickets?

918
00:38:24,950 --> 00:38:26,172
It really is 8:30.

919
00:38:26,172 --> 00:38:29,384
- [Joel] Can we have
the T-I-K-I-T-Z, please?

920
00:38:29,384 --> 00:38:32,217
- Alright, but turn the other way.

921
00:38:34,467 --> 00:38:38,570
- [Tom] Waitress, can we
order over here, please?

922
00:38:38,570 --> 00:38:40,541
- [Crow] Hey, while you're in
there, can I have a newspaper?

923
00:38:40,541 --> 00:38:42,181
- Here.

924
00:38:42,181 --> 00:38:43,120
- [Joel] Oh thanks.

925
00:38:43,120 --> 00:38:45,620
Hey, they're all warm and wet.

926
00:38:47,224 --> 00:38:49,216
- [Crow] Can I have my check, no I mean,

927
00:38:49,216 --> 00:38:51,966
can I bring you your check, yeah.

928
00:38:52,833 --> 00:38:55,917
- Trust me, you'll have lots
of time for that, eventually.

929
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:57,000
- [Crow] Huh?

930
00:38:58,978 --> 00:39:03,145
- [Joel] ♫ Driving along,
footloose and fancy free ♫

931
00:39:04,186 --> 00:39:05,811
- [Tom] Thank you for not smoking.

932
00:39:05,811 --> 00:39:07,231
- Mr. T,

933
00:39:07,231 --> 00:39:08,578
- [Joel] Move over.

934
00:39:08,578 --> 00:39:10,054
- I'm puzzled kind of.

935
00:39:10,054 --> 00:39:11,679
- [Crow] If there was only one gunman...

936
00:39:11,679 --> 00:39:13,159
- They're all creeps.

937
00:39:13,159 --> 00:39:14,690
- Creeps?

938
00:39:14,690 --> 00:39:16,408
- [Tom] You know, who committed
to reelect the President.

939
00:39:16,408 --> 00:39:17,865
- I simply don't get it.

940
00:39:17,865 --> 00:39:20,762
Here you form up a masterpiece, and then,

941
00:39:20,762 --> 00:39:24,039
with all the expert pros
available and on tap,

942
00:39:24,039 --> 00:39:26,136
you hire them creeps.

943
00:39:26,136 --> 00:39:27,297
Rank amateurs.

944
00:39:27,297 --> 00:39:28,875
- [Joel] I trust Howard Hunt, come on!

945
00:39:28,875 --> 00:39:30,700
- The exactly the crux of my plan.

946
00:39:30,700 --> 00:39:32,311
- [Tom] Don't say crux, please.

947
00:39:32,311 --> 00:39:35,520
- I excite the sleeping
ambition of half talented men,

948
00:39:35,520 --> 00:39:36,513
- [Crow] Thank you, sir.

949
00:39:36,513 --> 00:39:39,074
- Giving each of them a
glimpse of the promise land,

950
00:39:39,074 --> 00:39:42,086
the prospect of an hour of glory,

951
00:39:42,086 --> 00:39:45,478
lift them our of the drab and
hopeless swamp of mediocrity.

952
00:39:45,478 --> 00:39:47,023
- [Tom] You're hard to talk to, sir.

953
00:39:47,023 --> 00:39:50,618
- Once they're inspired by
this last chance to excel,

954
00:39:50,618 --> 00:39:52,462
the creeps, as you so poetically

955
00:39:52,462 --> 00:39:53,859
put it
- [Crow] Thank you.

956
00:39:53,859 --> 00:39:56,061
Will go on the mission with zeal

957
00:39:56,061 --> 00:39:59,367
and a single purpose unmatched
by even the most expert

958
00:39:59,367 --> 00:40:01,438
and practiced criminal.

959
00:40:01,438 --> 00:40:02,966
- [Crow] So, Hardy's okay with you?

960
00:40:02,966 --> 00:40:07,292
- That my good Sidney, is the
alpha and omega of my theory.

961
00:40:07,292 --> 00:40:10,478
The beginning and the
end of my psychology of

962
00:40:10,478 --> 00:40:12,327
directing the masterpiece of crime.

963
00:40:12,327 --> 00:40:15,253
- [Crow] You know, Burger
King has a drive-thru.

964
00:40:15,253 --> 00:40:17,214
(name drowned out by Crow's talking)

965
00:40:17,214 --> 00:40:18,131
- Who's he?

966
00:40:19,467 --> 00:40:21,521
- Another creep.

967
00:40:21,521 --> 00:40:23,969
- [Crow] My boss, always coming
up with phrases like that.

968
00:40:23,969 --> 00:40:24,927
- [Tom] Zing!

969
00:40:24,927 --> 00:40:26,832
- [Joel] It's the Flying Nun.

970
00:40:26,832 --> 00:40:27,665
- [Crow] It's Vertigo.

971
00:40:27,665 --> 00:40:30,114
- [Joel] It's Roman Holiday,
and much, much more.

972
00:40:30,114 --> 00:40:31,819
Now, after shopping we'll get some lunch,

973
00:40:31,819 --> 00:40:35,986
then it's off to the Robert
Hall store to get some shoes.

974
00:40:38,071 --> 00:40:40,081
- [Voiceover] Southern Pacific Sunset,

975
00:40:40,081 --> 00:40:42,014
arriving on track four.

976
00:40:42,014 --> 00:40:46,181
- [Joel] The remaining pizza
will go on sale for 15 cents.

977
00:40:47,203 --> 00:40:50,318
- [Crow] Now let's see,
Rubber Fantasy, Latex World,

978
00:40:50,318 --> 00:40:53,085
Butt Biters, and Newsweek, that'll do.

979
00:40:53,085 --> 00:40:55,902
Here's somethin' for you.

980
00:40:55,902 --> 00:40:57,927
- [Joel] Lee Harvey Oswald on vacation.

981
00:40:57,927 --> 00:40:59,481
- [Voiceover] Union Pacific Challenger,

982
00:40:59,481 --> 00:41:03,702
leaving on track five,
loading at gate number two.

983
00:41:03,702 --> 00:41:06,869
- [Crow] Visit the off world colonies.

984
00:41:08,593 --> 00:41:12,760
Whoops, just burped up a
little egg salad, whoops!

985
