00:52:17,501 --> 00:52:20,466
- [Crow] Oh, not a very good driver.

1225
00:52:20,466 --> 00:52:22,638
- [Joel] Thank God I had this helmet on.

1226
00:52:22,638 --> 00:52:24,624
- [Crow] I'm a mess.

1227
00:52:24,624 --> 00:52:25,981
Oh, that's right, I did that.

1228
00:52:25,981 --> 00:52:28,314
- [Joel] Shoulda worn a cup.

1229
00:52:33,414 --> 00:52:35,914
Must get to Benny Hill taping.

1230
00:52:38,294 --> 00:52:41,255
(door shuts)

1231
00:52:41,255 --> 00:52:42,149
- [Crow] You okay ma'am?

1232
00:52:42,149 --> 00:52:43,234
Uh, sir.

1233
00:52:43,234 --> 00:52:44,529
- [Tom] Yup, first thing
to do to a injured person,

1234
00:52:44,529 --> 00:52:45,905
move 'em.

1235
00:52:45,905 --> 00:52:46,740
(sirens)

1236
00:52:46,740 --> 00:52:47,970
- [Joel] I'm really in trouble now,

1237
00:52:47,970 --> 00:52:50,970
stay together Cheeks, stay together.

1238
00:52:52,829 --> 00:52:56,683
- [Crow] Hey, can I get a ride into town?

1239
00:52:56,683 --> 00:52:57,601
- What happened?

1240
00:52:57,601 --> 00:52:59,323
- Some dope ran me right off the road.

1241
00:52:59,323 --> 00:53:01,737
- [Joel] That was part of the plan.

1242
00:53:01,737 --> 00:53:03,786
- [Crow] Drawing their
guns at a traffic accident?

1243
00:53:03,786 --> 00:53:05,939
- You fellows sure came
along at the right time.

1244
00:53:05,939 --> 00:53:07,624
- [Joel] That's great, disrobe.

1245
00:53:07,624 --> 00:53:08,898
- I dunno where this guy came from,

1246
00:53:08,898 --> 00:53:10,877
but he looks pretty badly hurt to me.

1247
00:53:10,877 --> 00:53:12,501
- Try not to worry about him.

1248
00:53:12,501 --> 00:53:14,168
- Put your hands up.

1249
00:53:15,405 --> 00:53:18,072
- [Crow] And a new world record.

1250
00:53:19,589 --> 00:53:22,006
Whoa, it really got up there.

1251
00:53:23,622 --> 00:53:27,622
- [Joel] Oh man, they
rolled a Good Humor truck.

1252
00:53:29,017 --> 00:53:30,943
- Alright let's go, move!

1253
00:53:30,943 --> 00:53:32,235
- [Joel] We're gonna run it, too, huh?

1254
00:53:32,235 --> 00:53:33,068
Now I get it,

1255
00:53:33,068 --> 00:53:34,034
no wonder he had a helmet on.

1256
00:53:34,034 --> 00:53:35,721
- [Crow] You guys gonna
finish these sandwiches?

1257
00:53:35,721 --> 00:53:36,733
- [Joel] Now I left the house today with

1258
00:53:36,733 --> 00:53:39,715
a long rope, a medium
rope, and a short rope.

1259
00:53:39,715 --> 00:53:42,831
- [Tom] ♫ Oh it's a hap-hap-happy day ♫

1260
00:53:42,831 --> 00:53:45,164
(whistling)

1261
00:53:46,269 --> 00:53:49,191
Oh no, we robbed a diaper service.

1262
00:53:49,191 --> 00:53:50,522
- Lovely, lovely.

1263
00:53:50,522 --> 00:53:51,846
- Worked 'em like a clock.

1264
00:53:51,846 --> 00:53:53,538
A million buck clock.

1265
00:53:53,538 --> 00:53:54,422
- Let's move.

1266
00:53:54,422 --> 00:53:55,904
- [Crow] But I like where I'm livin'.

1267
00:53:55,904 --> 00:53:59,149
- [Joel] This is about the
time Superman would show up.

1268
00:53:59,149 --> 00:54:02,910
- [Tom] So, why don't they move
the car closer to the truck?

1269
00:54:02,910 --> 00:54:04,310
- A little assistance, gentlemen.

1270
00:54:04,310 --> 00:54:08,477
- [Joel] Whoops, I accidentally
tied up one of our gang.

1271
00:54:10,782 --> 00:54:12,167
- Can take three.

1272
00:54:12,167 --> 00:54:13,696
(sirens)

1273
00:54:13,696 --> 00:54:14,699
- [Crow] Is that us?

1274
00:54:14,699 --> 00:54:16,616
- That's it, lets move.

1275
00:54:20,353 --> 00:54:22,589
- [Joel] Can I ride in front, Boss?

1276
00:54:22,589 --> 00:54:24,062
- [Tom] I'm thirsty, who's thirsty?

1277
00:54:24,062 --> 00:54:26,777
I've gotta Mountain Dew,
Diet Coke, Mr. Pibb..

1278
00:54:26,777 --> 00:54:29,527
- [Crow] Hey, hand me my slurpee.

1279
00:54:32,519 --> 00:54:35,825
- [Joel] Hey, Wally, we need
some shocks on this thing.

1280
00:54:35,825 --> 00:54:37,745
Ridin' kinda low.

1281
00:54:37,745 --> 00:54:41,373
- [Crow] The Blue Ridge
Mountains of Chicago.

1282
00:54:41,373 --> 00:54:43,153
- [Joel] Hey look, they drove onto the

1283
00:54:43,153 --> 00:54:44,820
Timmy and Lasse set.

1284
00:54:46,559 --> 00:54:50,421
- [Tom] You shoulda gone before the heist.

1285
00:54:50,421 --> 00:54:54,588
- [Joel] What a rush, they
totally don't know where we are.

1286
00:54:55,856 --> 00:54:58,167
- [Crow] An Ed Asner costume.

1287
00:54:58,167 --> 00:54:59,183
- We're five minutes behind schedule,

1288
00:54:59,183 --> 00:55:00,683
I suggest beat it.

1289
00:55:02,479 --> 00:55:03,312
- [Tom] Alright,

1290
00:55:03,312 --> 00:55:04,145
♫ Happy Birthday to me,

1291
00:55:04,145 --> 00:55:04,994
♫ Happy Birthday to me ♫

1292
00:55:04,994 --> 00:55:06,411
I shouldn't have.

1293
00:55:09,741 --> 00:55:12,824
- [Crow] Ha, he's buildin' a lean to.

1294
00:55:14,945 --> 00:55:17,300
- [Tom] Mr. Goodbars?

1295
00:55:17,300 --> 00:55:18,888
- [Joel] Hey, I found
some roots and grubs.

1296
00:55:18,888 --> 00:55:20,972
We could survive here for weeks.

1297
00:55:20,972 --> 00:55:24,555
(dramatic orchestra music)

1298
00:55:27,588 --> 00:55:29,919
- All the guns go into the hole as well.

1299
00:55:29,919 --> 00:55:33,544
- [Crow] Fire in the hole, ah nevermind.

1300
00:55:33,544 --> 00:55:34,857
- [Joel] So where's this go?

1301
00:55:34,857 --> 00:55:36,180
- [Crow[ In The Hole.

1302
00:55:36,180 --> 00:55:39,004
Movie's not over yet and
their strikin' the set.

1303
00:55:39,004 --> 00:55:40,407
- [Tom] Okay, what about this?

1304
00:55:40,407 --> 00:55:41,852
- [Joel] That would go in the hole.

1305
00:55:41,852 --> 00:55:42,935
- [Tom] Okay.

1306
00:55:44,156 --> 00:55:48,156
- [Crow] Lets see, hole,
hole, garage sale, hole

1307
00:55:49,458 --> 00:55:51,625
hole, Salvation Army, hole

1308
00:55:53,067 --> 00:55:54,143
- [Tom] Where's the turtle wax?

1309
00:55:54,143 --> 00:55:55,893
- [Joel] In the hole!

1310
00:55:57,479 --> 00:55:58,832
- [Tom] Kettle drum?

1311
00:55:58,832 --> 00:56:00,582
- [Joel] In the hole.

1312
00:56:04,239 --> 00:56:05,072
- [Tom] Hole, right?

1313
00:56:05,072 --> 00:56:06,237
- [Joel] Yup.

1314
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:07,070
- [Tom] That?

1315
00:56:07,070 --> 00:56:07,982
- [Joel] In the hole.

1316
00:56:07,982 --> 00:56:09,627
- That stays with me.

1317
00:56:09,627 --> 00:56:13,210
(dramatic orchestra music)

1318
00:56:17,748 --> 00:56:22,633
- [Crow] Oh yeah, it's so
easy to find cop appliques.

1319
00:56:22,633 --> 00:56:23,601
- [Tom] Where's that go?

1320
00:56:23,601 --> 00:56:25,213
- [Joel] In the hole.

1321
00:56:25,213 --> 00:56:27,904
- [Tom] Belt, pants, heck I'm
just gonna jump in the hole.

1322
00:56:27,904 --> 00:56:28,737
(laughing)

1323
00:56:28,737 --> 00:56:30,552
(staccato piano music)

1324
00:56:30,552 --> 00:56:32,086
- [Joel] Could you look under the hood,

1325
00:56:32,086 --> 00:56:34,644
there's some funny sound comin' out of it?

1326
00:56:34,644 --> 00:56:36,613
- [Tom] Tell Zappa to turn the music down,

1327
00:56:36,613 --> 00:56:38,405
Ruth Underwood wants her vibes back.

1328
00:56:38,405 --> 00:56:41,030
(staccato piano music)

1329
00:56:41,030 --> 00:56:45,030
- [Crow] Be sure to put
that shovel in the hole.

1330
00:56:47,579 --> 00:56:48,633
- [Joel] Alright, who wants gum?

1331
00:56:48,633 --> 00:56:50,221
- [Crow] I do, I do.
- [Tom] I do, I do.

1332
00:56:50,221 --> 00:56:51,415
- [Joel] In the hole.

1333
00:56:51,415 --> 00:56:52,585
- You have exactly 30 minutes to get back

1334
00:56:52,585 --> 00:56:54,260
to the train, gentlemen.

1335
00:56:54,260 --> 00:56:55,350
- [Joel] And have your tickets ready,

1336
00:56:55,350 --> 00:56:57,319
they're real strict about that.

1337
00:56:57,319 --> 00:56:59,342
(loud drumming music)

1338
00:56:59,342 --> 00:57:01,568
Hey, I was supposed to
get the front this time.

1339
00:57:01,568 --> 00:57:04,006
- [Tom] But I get carsick,
you don't want that.

1340
00:57:04,006 --> 00:57:06,374
(door shutting)

1341
00:57:06,374 --> 00:57:07,207
- [Crow] You idiot,

1342
00:57:07,207 --> 00:57:09,846
your coat is stuck in that door again.

1343
00:57:09,846 --> 00:57:12,502
- [Tom] We can't get it out of reverse!

1344
00:57:12,502 --> 00:57:13,335
- [Crow] I just don't understand

1345
00:57:13,335 --> 00:57:14,898
the rebel part of this movie.

1346
00:57:14,898 --> 00:57:17,200
- [Joel] Well, robbing a
bank was pretty rebellious.

1347
00:57:17,200 --> 00:57:18,367
- [Crow] Yeah.

1348
00:57:20,599 --> 00:57:25,116
- [Tom] I used up that
dollar three hours ago.

1349
00:57:25,116 --> 00:57:28,224
- [Crow] Hey, she got a new head torte.

1350
00:57:28,224 --> 00:57:31,307
- [Tom] Pardon me, boy, oh forget it.

1351
00:57:34,845 --> 00:57:37,070
- [Joel] It looks like
she bought a snare drum.

1352
00:57:37,070 --> 00:57:37,903
- What took you so long.

1353
00:57:37,903 --> 00:57:38,736
- I made it, didn't I?

1354
00:57:38,736 --> 00:57:39,569
Come on.

1355
00:57:41,766 --> 00:57:44,427
- [Crow] I said, have your tickets ready.

1356
00:57:44,427 --> 00:57:48,081
- Hey Lelund, I'm Jack
Simpson, Chicago Morning Star.

1357
00:57:48,081 --> 00:57:51,479
- Why don't you guys leave me alone?

1358
00:57:51,479 --> 00:57:53,270
- How 'bout your mother?

1359
00:57:53,270 --> 00:57:56,072
There's a rumor Count
Opheno gave her the heir.

1360
00:57:56,072 --> 00:57:57,104
- Get outta my way.

1361
00:57:57,104 --> 00:57:58,304
- Listen, buster.

1362
00:57:58,304 --> 00:57:59,377
- [Tom] I hate her.

1363
00:57:59,377 --> 00:58:01,056
- You know, you could use
a little more good will

1364
00:58:01,056 --> 00:58:02,306
from the press.

1365
00:58:05,374 --> 00:58:07,394
- [Joel] So anyway, I
bought this darling drum

1366
00:58:07,394 --> 00:58:08,867
and it's got the snare and everything,

1367
00:58:08,867 --> 00:58:10,819
I don't see why we couldn't...

1368
00:58:10,819 --> 00:58:11,652
- [Crow] Hey, it's Ralph!

1369
00:58:11,652 --> 00:58:13,499
She's takin' the Hooterville trolley, too.

1370
00:58:13,499 --> 00:58:15,087
(startled screaming)

1371
00:58:15,087 --> 00:58:17,182
- [Tom] The Exorcist.

1372
00:58:17,182 --> 00:58:19,529
- [Crow] Flat point.

1373
00:58:19,529 --> 00:58:21,555
- How was your meeting?

1374
00:58:21,555 --> 00:58:23,222
- [Crow] Profitable.

1375
00:58:24,776 --> 00:58:25,609
- Johnny?

1376
00:58:27,421 --> 00:58:28,554
- Oh, my meeting?

1377
00:58:28,554 --> 00:58:29,963
- [Joel] Why can't Johnny fight?

1378
00:58:29,963 --> 00:58:30,896
- It went fine.

1379
00:58:30,896 --> 00:58:33,650
- You don't sound very enthusiastic.

1380
00:58:33,650 --> 00:58:35,374
- It was not very exciting
meeting a play write.

1381
00:58:35,374 --> 00:58:37,993
- Oh, I thought it was
one of the money people?

1382
00:58:37,993 --> 00:58:40,126
- Well, he's a rich play write.

1383
00:58:40,126 --> 00:58:42,212
- Oh, what's his name?
- [Joel] Rich.

1384
00:58:42,212 --> 00:58:43,832
- What is this a cross examination?

1385
00:58:43,832 --> 00:58:46,000
- [Crow] Nobody expects
to cross examine...

1386
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:47,214
(training bumping)

1387
00:58:47,214 --> 00:58:48,538
- [Joel] Oh, sorry.

1388
00:58:48,538 --> 00:58:51,205
(train whistle)

1389
00:58:52,212 --> 00:58:53,449
- I'm sorry, honey.

1390
00:58:53,449 --> 00:58:54,282
- [Joel] I'm a jerk, you know that!

1391
00:58:54,282 --> 00:58:56,848
- I guess my nerves are on edge a bit.

1392
00:58:56,848 --> 00:58:59,675
- [Crow] George Bernard
Shaw was teasing me.

1393
00:58:59,675 --> 00:59:02,114
- His name was Sal Houston.

1394
00:59:02,114 --> 00:59:05,327
- [Joel] Yeah, a big
Jew from Texas, whoops.

1395
00:59:05,327 --> 00:59:06,915
- That's the man you said
you met in Hollywood.

1396
00:59:06,915 --> 00:59:08,434
- [Tom] No, that was
the other Sal Houston.

1397
00:59:08,434 --> 00:59:10,030
The Chicago one.

1398
00:59:10,030 --> 00:59:11,372
- Yeah, that's right.

1399
00:59:11,372 --> 00:59:14,464
I meant to tell you, honey,
he flew in yesterday.

1400
00:59:14,464 --> 00:59:18,142
- [Joel] We'll never use
the closets in our house.

1401
00:59:18,142 --> 00:59:21,225
(upbeat dance music)

1402
00:59:25,954 --> 00:59:26,937
- Excuse me, Mr. Miller.

1403
00:59:26,937 --> 00:59:29,527
- [Joel] Love Tropic of
Cancer, just had to tell ya.

1404
00:59:29,527 --> 00:59:30,689
- [Crow] Hey, it's Merritt Stone.

1405
00:59:30,689 --> 00:59:31,522
- [Tom] No it isn't.

1406
00:59:31,522 --> 00:59:32,368
- [Crow] Yes it is.

1407
00:59:32,368 --> 00:59:34,057
- [Tom] It's not.

1408
00:59:34,057 --> 00:59:36,639
- You're a writer, eh?

1409
00:59:36,639 --> 00:59:37,973
- [Joel] I guess not.

1410
00:59:37,973 --> 00:59:39,118
- If I could just sit down

1411
00:59:39,118 --> 00:59:40,593
all the true-to-life things I've see.

1412
00:59:40,593 --> 00:59:41,636
- [Crow] You'd throw up.

1413
00:59:41,636 --> 00:59:43,541
- But you and me could.

1414
00:59:43,541 --> 00:59:45,046
You are a writer, aren't you?

1415
00:59:45,046 --> 00:59:48,098
- [Joel] Yeah, I write
about the life of the mind.

1416
00:59:48,098 --> 00:59:50,358
- You know, everybody I've
told about my memoir says,

1417
00:59:50,358 --> 00:59:52,399
- write a book.
- [Joel] Shut up.

1418
00:59:52,399 --> 00:59:55,388
- [Tom] Like, I once saw a
woman with an unusual hat.

1419
00:59:55,388 --> 00:59:58,176
- The same thing's happened to me.

1420
00:59:58,176 --> 01:00:00,009
- I wish I could type.

1421
01:00:01,192 --> 01:00:02,859
Say, here's my card.

1422
01:00:04,709 --> 01:00:07,142
50/50 on all my stories, alright?

1423
01:00:07,142 --> 01:00:09,754
- [Crow] Thank you,
Mr. Animal Rummy is it?

1424
01:00:09,754 --> 01:00:11,421
- Thanks Mr. Miller.

1425
01:00:12,510 --> 01:00:14,452
- I'll call you.

1426
01:00:14,452 --> 01:00:16,518
- Thanks a lot.

1427
01:00:16,518 --> 01:00:18,528
- [Joel] I'll bet he never called.

1428
01:00:18,528 --> 01:00:19,688
Now let's see, where was I?

1429
01:00:19,688 --> 01:00:21,656
A screaming comes across the sky.

1430
01:00:21,656 --> 01:00:23,315
- [Voiceover] As of this
hour, the police have no leads

1431
01:00:23,315 --> 01:00:25,064
as to the armored car robbery in Chicago.

1432
01:00:25,064 --> 01:00:28,647
- [Joel] Hey, turn it
up, this is my heist.

1433
01:00:30,636 --> 01:00:32,142
So, you gals are in a band?

1434
01:00:32,142 --> 01:00:33,142
We're Heart.

1435
01:00:34,847 --> 01:00:38,934
- Reverend, do you know
what I think is responsible

1436
01:00:38,934 --> 01:00:40,587
for all of this crime?

1437
01:00:40,587 --> 01:00:41,674
- [Crow] Eisenhower.

1438
01:00:41,674 --> 01:00:44,273
- I haven't the most
remote idea Sister Petchal.

1439
01:00:44,273 --> 01:00:46,106
- The people involved.

1440
01:00:47,163 --> 01:00:48,567
- [Tom] Our link letter,

1441
01:00:48,567 --> 01:00:50,505
they all have our link letter on 'em.

1442
01:00:50,505 --> 01:00:51,338
- Who is it?

1443
01:00:51,338 --> 01:00:52,308
- [Tom] Just a second.

1444
01:00:52,308 --> 01:00:55,280
Hold on I'm countin'
all the loot we stole.

1445
01:00:55,280 --> 01:00:57,947
Whoops, sorry I didn't say that.

1446
01:01:00,221 --> 01:01:01,663
- [Crow] Got the five bucks you owe me?

1447
01:01:01,663 --> 01:01:04,179
I wanna get some chips.

1448
01:01:04,179 --> 01:01:05,658
- [Joel] Art Linkletter.

1449
01:01:05,658 --> 01:01:07,306
- Isn't it?

1450
01:01:07,306 --> 01:01:08,386
- [Crow] Kinda cute?

1451
01:01:08,386 --> 01:01:09,806
- What're you doin' with a gun?

1452
01:01:09,806 --> 01:01:11,509
- Just keepin' it company.

1453
01:01:11,509 --> 01:01:13,139
- What's the matter with you?

1454
01:01:13,139 --> 01:01:15,267
Tucker warned us about guns.

1455
01:01:15,267 --> 01:01:17,804
- I need a gun to protect
my beautiful money.

1456
01:01:17,804 --> 01:01:19,404
- Your money?

1457
01:01:19,404 --> 01:01:22,321
- [Crow] It's for my student loans.

1458
01:01:24,622 --> 01:01:26,765
- [Joel] Think fast.
- There's your cut.

1459
01:01:26,765 --> 01:01:28,419
Now you get outta here.

1460
01:01:28,419 --> 01:01:31,284
- You don't think you're
gonna get away this?

1461
01:01:31,284 --> 01:01:33,514
- The only thing you can
do is yell for the cops,

1462
01:01:33,514 --> 01:01:36,761
but you won't do that, not
with your beautiful wife.

1463
01:01:36,761 --> 01:01:39,928
- [Tom] This is not my beautiful wife.

1464
01:01:40,784 --> 01:01:42,857
Yes I can certainly see where
you'd wanna keep that money.

1465
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:45,242
I can certainly side with your
side of the argument here.

1466
01:01:45,242 --> 01:01:46,241
No doubt about it.

1467
01:01:46,241 --> 01:01:48,285
(crashing)

1468
01:01:48,285 --> 01:01:50,340
- [Crow] This is just like
Treasure of the Sierra Madre,

1469
01:01:50,340 --> 01:01:51,923
only it's not good.

1470
01:01:54,861 --> 01:01:59,028
(humming an upbeat, dramatic song)

1471
01:02:01,510 --> 01:02:03,677
(banging)

1472
01:02:06,232 --> 01:02:10,929
- [Joel] Now, to return
this to Marshall Fields.

1473
01:02:10,929 --> 01:02:14,551
- [Crow] Goodbye, nice workin' with ya.

1474
01:02:14,551 --> 01:02:17,061
(door opening and shutting)

1475
01:02:17,061 --> 01:02:19,807
- I don't see that Lelund boy anywhere.

1476
01:02:19,807 --> 01:02:21,518
- Probably drinkin' his dinner.

1477
01:02:21,518 --> 01:02:23,505
- Oh Hattie you know very well

1478
01:02:23,505 --> 01:02:27,129
it's not drinkin' that
got him into the papers.

1479
01:02:27,129 --> 01:02:28,379
- [Tom] Donuts?

1480
01:02:32,134 --> 01:02:33,448
- [Crow] Pst, come on.

1481
01:02:33,448 --> 01:02:34,534
It's about the heist.

1482
01:02:34,534 --> 01:02:35,367
- [Joel] My waist?

1483
01:02:35,367 --> 01:02:37,284
- [Crow] No, the heist.

1484
01:02:39,800 --> 01:02:40,633
- Reverend?

1485
01:02:40,633 --> 01:02:42,603
- [Joel] Blue Jeans.

1486
01:02:42,603 --> 01:02:45,186
(door opening)

1487
01:02:46,569 --> 01:02:48,969
(train bell ringing)

1488
01:02:48,969 --> 01:02:49,961
You bitch.

1489
01:02:49,961 --> 01:02:50,936
- What are you doing with that?

1490
01:02:50,936 --> 01:02:52,366
- I've just had a fight with George.

1491
01:02:52,366 --> 01:02:53,302
I had to slug him.

1492
01:02:53,302 --> 01:02:54,429
- [Crow] It was so freeing.

1493
01:02:54,429 --> 01:02:55,766
- Thieves falling out?

1494
01:02:55,766 --> 01:02:58,181
- He wanted to keep all
the money for himself.

1495
01:02:58,181 --> 01:03:01,046
- I don't want it here,
what about your compartment?

1496
01:03:01,046 --> 01:03:03,338
- And have Jeanne find it?

1497
01:03:03,338 --> 01:03:04,299
- I don't want it here.

1498
01:03:04,299 --> 01:03:05,444
- What do you suggest?

1499
01:03:05,444 --> 01:03:07,963
We call the conductor and
have him keep it for us?

1500
01:03:07,963 --> 01:03:09,483
- [Tom] You know I didn't mean that.

1501
01:03:09,483 --> 01:03:12,646
- You've gotta talk
some sense into George.

1502
01:03:12,646 --> 01:03:14,156
- [Joel] I can't stay mad at you.

1503
01:03:14,156 --> 01:03:15,656
Come on let's hug.

1504
01:03:20,999 --> 01:03:22,661
- [Crow] Mickey Mouse.

1505
01:03:22,661 --> 01:03:24,328
- [Joel] M-U-R-D-E-R

1506
01:03:28,144 --> 01:03:29,214
- [Tom] I see your point,

1507
01:03:29,214 --> 01:03:31,400
but if we do hide the loot in my room,

1508
01:03:31,400 --> 01:03:33,810
then the cops might find it
and then we're gonna be...

1509
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:38,296
- [Crow] He's got a nice
round one, doesn't he?

1510
01:03:38,296 --> 01:03:41,046
- [Joel] It's Floyd Terbone, hmm.

1511
01:03:43,593 --> 01:03:46,467
- [Crow] Well, we're
rebels, here's our chance.

1512
01:03:46,467 --> 01:03:49,620
Disturb, disturb, disturb, disturb.

1513
01:03:49,620 --> 01:03:50,453
- [Tom] Is he bugging you?

1514
01:03:50,453 --> 01:03:51,960
- [Joel] No.

1515
01:03:51,960 --> 01:03:53,184
He's a mess.

1516
01:03:53,184 --> 01:03:55,664
- [Tom] Chocolate mess.

1517
01:03:55,664 --> 01:03:59,910
- [Crow] (sniffing) Steve, Steve!

1518
01:03:59,910 --> 01:04:03,584
- [Joel] Yuck, good
thing the carpet's brown.

1519
01:04:03,584 --> 01:04:04,696
- You forgot to mention one thing,

1520
01:04:04,696 --> 01:04:06,723
you put a bullet through his brain.

1521
01:04:06,723 --> 01:04:07,833
- All I did was hit 'em.

1522
01:04:07,833 --> 01:04:09,846
- [Joel] It was a bullet.

1523
01:04:09,846 --> 01:04:11,889
- I didn't use a gun.

1524
01:04:11,889 --> 01:04:13,621
This is the one I took from him.

1525
01:04:13,621 --> 01:04:15,704
Take a look for yourself.

1526
01:04:17,500 --> 01:04:19,873
- [Joel] Hmm, kids, shot this guy for you.

1527
01:04:19,873 --> 01:04:21,489
Ham in fridge, Mom.

1528
01:04:21,489 --> 01:04:23,072
- Suicide.

1529
01:04:23,072 --> 01:04:26,250
- Except that looks type written.

1530
01:04:26,250 --> 01:04:27,386
And I got gun.

1531
01:04:27,386 --> 01:04:28,517
- [Crow] I got gun.

1532
01:04:28,517 --> 01:04:30,650
- You know who's typewriter
that was written on?

1533
01:04:30,650 --> 01:04:31,932
Mine!

1534
01:04:31,932 --> 01:04:33,460
The "e" on my typewriter prints lower

1535
01:04:33,460 --> 01:04:34,598
than the rest of the letters.

1536
01:04:34,598 --> 01:04:36,106
- [Crow] Wow!

1537
01:04:36,106 --> 01:04:36,939
- Let's get out of here.

1538
01:04:36,939 --> 01:04:38,849
- No.
- [Joel] No?

1539
01:04:38,849 --> 01:04:40,588
They could trace that note to me.

1540
01:04:40,588 --> 01:04:42,559
- He's tried committing suicide before.

1541
01:04:42,559 --> 01:04:43,920
- [Tom] Did it work?

1542
01:04:43,920 --> 01:04:45,973
- You could get rid of your typewriter.

1543
01:04:45,973 --> 01:04:46,898
- That would mean that only you and I know

1544
01:04:46,898 --> 01:04:49,247
that it was murder.

1545
01:04:49,247 --> 01:04:50,480
- I think you're forgetting someone else.

1546
01:04:50,480 --> 01:04:52,449
- [Crow] God knows, Davey.

1547
01:04:52,449 --> 01:04:53,482
- Who?

1548
01:04:53,482 --> 01:04:54,315
- The murderer.

1549
01:04:54,315 --> 01:04:55,575
(laughing)

1550
01:04:55,575 --> 01:04:56,944
- [Joel] Oh no, it's a social gospel.

1551
01:04:56,944 --> 01:04:59,041
- I quite agree with you Sister Ventura.

1552
01:04:59,041 --> 01:05:01,184
Mine too is a small town.

1553
01:05:01,184 --> 01:05:03,900
Yet somehow, in such
Arcadian surroundings,

1554
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:06,850
sin doesn't seem to be quite so sinful.

1555
01:05:06,850 --> 01:05:08,868
- How true, how true.

1556
01:05:08,868 --> 01:05:12,451
- [Tom] Travelling with
Gertrude and Alice.

1557
01:05:13,354 --> 01:05:15,325
- [Crow] Yeah, but I still
say if we hid the loot

1558
01:05:15,325 --> 01:05:18,549
with the body that'd be killing
two birds with one stone.

1559
01:05:18,549 --> 01:05:22,090
- Those two men look as though
they've just seen a ghost.

1560
01:05:22,090 --> 01:05:23,327
- How many men are afraid of ghosts

1561
01:05:23,327 --> 01:05:25,881
who are not afraid of the all high?

1562
01:05:25,881 --> 01:05:28,421
- You put that very beautifully, Reverend.

1563
01:05:28,421 --> 01:05:29,254
- [Joel] But shut up.

1564
01:05:29,254 --> 01:05:30,254
- Thank you.

1565
01:05:31,194 --> 01:05:32,454
(door slamming)

1566
01:05:32,454 --> 01:05:33,391
Oh my knee, oh jeez.

1567
01:05:33,391 --> 01:05:35,459
- [Tom] Oh, that's better.

1568
01:05:35,459 --> 01:05:36,957
- I think I better get back to Jeanne

1569
01:05:36,957 --> 01:05:38,839
before she starts worrying.

1570
01:05:38,839 --> 01:05:41,331
- I'll get rid of the typewriter.

1571
01:05:41,331 --> 01:05:42,703
- [Crow] Where's my kiss?

1572
01:05:42,703 --> 01:05:44,286
What about my kiss?

1573
01:05:48,618 --> 01:05:50,095
- [Joel] I still suck,

1574
01:05:50,095 --> 01:05:51,544
I thought I had written
something good for a second,

1575
01:05:51,544 --> 01:05:52,961
I don't know why.

1576
01:05:55,181 --> 01:05:59,901
Gordon Lish is gonna give me
a really bad grade for this.

1577
01:05:59,901 --> 01:06:02,621
- [Tom] ♫ Summer breeze,
makes me feel fine,

1578
01:06:02,621 --> 01:06:06,788
♫ Goin' through the jasmine ♫

1579
01:06:09,832 --> 01:06:11,522
As a gift to the reading public,

1580
01:06:11,522 --> 01:06:13,854
he's throwing his typewriter away.

1581
01:06:13,854 --> 01:06:15,076
Thank you.

1582
01:06:15,076 --> 01:06:17,107
- [Crow] He thinks he's Harry Truman.

1583
01:06:17,107 --> 01:06:21,057
- [Tom] I'll just drop these in the mail.

1584
01:06:21,057 --> 01:06:22,733
- [Joel] Ow!

1585
01:06:22,733 --> 01:06:23,900
- [Tom] Sorry!

1586
01:06:25,727 --> 01:06:26,719
- [Joel] Man, I wish Bret Easton Ellis

1587
01:06:26,719 --> 01:06:28,740
would do that with his typewriter.

1588
01:06:28,740 --> 01:06:30,293
- [Tom] Yeah.
- [Crow] Yup.

1589
01:06:30,293 --> 01:06:33,043
- [Tom] So, do I come here often?

1590
01:06:33,923 --> 01:06:36,503
- Very clever Mr. Miller.

1591
01:06:36,503 --> 01:06:39,346
A wise precaution on your part.

1592
01:06:39,346 --> 01:06:40,332
- Who are you?

1593
01:06:40,332 --> 01:06:42,569
- I'm the Reverend Basal Cunningham,

1594
01:06:42,569 --> 01:06:45,880
or should I say the very Reverend.

1595
01:06:45,880 --> 01:06:47,483
- You're Tucker!

1596
01:06:47,483 --> 01:06:48,958
- [Crow] We just did a
heist together, remember?

1597
01:06:48,958 --> 01:06:50,355
- I'm the Reverend Basal Cunningham

1598
01:06:50,355 --> 01:06:51,922
of Penbrook, New Hampshire.

1599
01:06:51,922 --> 01:06:53,976
- [Tom] I believe, you
believe, that's who you are.

1600
01:06:53,976 --> 01:06:55,097
- I should have known
you'd never let that money

1601
01:06:55,097 --> 01:06:57,280
get too far away from you.

1602
01:06:57,280 --> 01:06:59,995
You're the one who killed George!

1603
01:06:59,995 --> 01:07:01,616
- One less share to disperse.

1604
01:07:01,616 --> 01:07:03,398
- [Tom] One less spell to ask.

1605
01:07:03,398 --> 01:07:04,700
- And now Mr. Miller

1606
01:07:04,700 --> 01:07:07,018
- [Crow] I'm gonna shave your mustache.

1607
01:07:07,018 --> 01:07:09,989
- There'll be still another share less.

1608
01:07:09,989 --> 01:07:11,796
- [Crow] Cross and a switchblade.

1609
01:07:11,796 --> 01:07:13,472
- You don't have to kill me.

1610
01:07:13,472 --> 01:07:16,067
- [Crow] Murder on the Dis-Orient Express.

1611
01:07:16,067 --> 01:07:18,094
- I don't want any of your damn money!

1612
01:07:18,094 --> 01:07:20,233
(train horn)

1613
01:07:20,233 --> 01:07:21,569
- [Crow] So hey, what happened?

1614
01:07:21,569 --> 01:07:22,819
I don't get it.

1615
01:07:24,372 --> 01:07:25,479
- Conductor!

1616
01:07:25,479 --> 01:07:26,759
- [Crow] I'm lonely.

1617
01:07:26,759 --> 01:07:27,866
- Are we on time?

1618
01:07:27,866 --> 01:07:28,765
- Why yes we are.

1619
01:07:28,765 --> 01:07:30,193
- We hate to be late.

1620
01:07:30,193 --> 01:07:31,302
- So do we.

1621
01:07:31,302 --> 01:07:33,405
Now if you'll excuse me
I have some work to do.

1622
01:07:33,405 --> 01:07:37,471
- I think lateness is a defect
in a person's character.

1623
01:07:37,471 --> 01:07:40,228
- This train is never late, goodnight.

1624
01:07:40,228 --> 01:07:43,458
- [Joel] Gary Busey after the accident.

1625
01:07:43,458 --> 01:07:45,227
- [Crow] Bookends.

1626
01:07:45,227 --> 01:07:47,866
- He's a disgrace to the uniform.

1627
01:07:47,866 --> 01:07:52,020
- [Crow] I love a disgrace to an uniform.

1628
01:07:52,020 --> 01:07:53,812
- The air conditioning on
this train is splendid,

1629
01:07:53,812 --> 01:07:57,055
but there's nothing like
God's own air to breathe.

1630
01:07:57,055 --> 01:07:59,425
- Well maybe so, Reverend,
- [Crow] So out you go.

1631
01:07:59,425 --> 01:08:00,485
But it's against regulations.

1632
01:08:00,485 --> 01:08:03,280
- Regulations against breathing?

1633
01:08:03,280 --> 01:08:05,628
- You all have your little
joke, do you Reverend?

1634
01:08:05,628 --> 01:08:06,586
- [Tom] You make me sick.

1635
01:08:06,586 --> 01:08:08,217
- [Joel] Why don't we go?

1636
01:08:08,217 --> 01:08:09,076
- Goodnight, Reverend.

1637
01:08:09,076 --> 01:08:11,803
- Goodnight to you, sir.
- [Crow] What a dope.

1638
01:08:11,803 --> 01:08:14,551
(train engine)

1639
01:08:14,551 --> 01:08:17,218
(doors closing)

1640
01:08:22,117 --> 01:08:24,065
- Joel, we got our short stories ready.

1641
01:08:24,065 --> 01:08:24,939
I'm so excited.

1642
01:08:24,939 --> 01:08:27,322
Having a writer's
workshop was a great idea.

1643
01:08:27,322 --> 01:08:28,992
I may even give up
writing spec scripts and

1644
01:08:28,992 --> 01:08:31,482
concentrate solely on fiction from now on.

1645
01:08:31,482 --> 01:08:32,633
- Oh that's great Crow.

1646
01:08:32,633 --> 01:08:35,630
It's open up a whole new area
of writing for you to fail in.

1647
01:08:35,630 --> 01:08:37,662
- That's not very supportive, Tom.

1648
01:08:37,662 --> 01:08:38,860
- [Joel] Thank you.
- Yeah, whatever.

1649
01:08:38,860 --> 01:08:39,985
Joel, what made you decide to have this

1650
01:08:39,985 --> 01:08:41,689
dumb ole' writer's workshop anyway?

1651
01:08:41,689 --> 01:08:43,964
- Well it's from this new
creative writing book I got

1652
01:08:43,964 --> 01:08:46,220
Called, Writing Down the
Tracks, by Merritt Stone,

1653
01:08:46,220 --> 01:08:48,324
the conductor in today's experiment.

1654
01:08:48,324 --> 01:08:49,996
- He's not Merritt Stone.

1655
01:08:49,996 --> 01:08:51,906
- Whatever, let's here
your stories you guys.

1656
01:08:51,906 --> 01:08:54,776
- Okay, me first, me first.

1657
01:08:54,776 --> 01:08:57,134
The vast emptiness of space lay before me.

1658
01:08:57,134 --> 01:09:00,269
The star and the galaxies
were apart from me,

1659
01:09:00,269 --> 01:09:02,399
yet seemed inside me also.

1660
01:09:02,399 --> 01:09:03,987
All of my deepest yearnings,

1661
01:09:03,987 --> 01:09:06,476
my most profound inner most thoughts,

1662
01:09:06,476 --> 01:09:08,734
my striving, aching sole that
longed to love and be loved,

1663
01:09:08,734 --> 01:09:11,660
all of these things were reflected

1664
01:09:11,660 --> 01:09:13,771
in the twinkling of the stars,

1665
01:09:13,771 --> 01:09:15,879
the rising of the moon as I venture...

1666
01:09:15,879 --> 01:09:18,762
- Uh, Crow listen, that's
all very well and good

1667
01:09:18,762 --> 01:09:20,261
but if Merritt Stone were here...

1668
01:09:20,261 --> 01:09:22,224
- [Tom] He's not Merritt Stone.

1669
01:09:22,224 --> 01:09:24,599
- If Merritt Stone were
here he would wonder why

1670
01:09:24,599 --> 01:09:27,028
there's no scene where
a ticket get punched,

1671
01:09:27,028 --> 01:09:31,244
and no one has said, "Can
I take your bags, please?"

1672
01:09:31,244 --> 01:09:33,195
As far as I can tell,

1673
01:09:33,195 --> 01:09:35,209
your story doesn't even involve a train,

1674
01:09:35,209 --> 01:09:39,340
I'm sorry Crow, this is gonna
need extensive re-writes

1675
01:09:39,340 --> 01:09:41,459
if you wanna please Merritt Stone.

1676
01:09:41,459 --> 01:09:42,292
Tom?

1677
01:09:42,292 --> 01:09:44,287
- He's not Merritt Stone, thank you.

1678
01:09:44,287 --> 01:09:46,925
A stately, plump Buck Mulligan
came down from the stairwell

1679
01:09:46,925 --> 01:09:49,700
and laid a razor on the...

1680
01:09:49,700 --> 01:09:51,205
- Hey, you stole that from Joyce Dewitt.

1681
01:09:51,205 --> 01:09:54,904
- Crow, it's James Joyce and
whether he stole it, or not,

1682
01:09:54,904 --> 01:09:57,151
his story has no sense of place.

1683
01:09:57,151 --> 01:10:00,547
We have no idea if it takes
place in Massapequa Park,

1684
01:10:00,547 --> 01:10:03,797
Amityville, Copage Lindenhurst, Babylon

1685
01:10:04,824 --> 01:10:06,875
♫ Change a Jamaica for a ♫

1686
01:10:06,875 --> 01:10:10,517
- [Crow] That doesn't, ugh.
- That doesn't, ahhh.

1687
01:10:10,517 --> 01:10:11,975
- Can I read my story?

1688
01:10:11,975 --> 01:10:13,892
- Sure Gypsy, go ahead.

1689
01:10:15,238 --> 01:10:18,905
- A train leaves a
station at two p.m. going

1690
01:10:20,023 --> 01:10:21,600
90 miles an hour.

1691
01:10:21,600 --> 01:10:24,200
Another train leaves another station

1692
01:10:24,200 --> 01:10:27,192
going the opposite
direction at five p.m. going

1693
01:10:27,192 --> 01:10:28,609
60 miles an hour.

1694
01:10:29,698 --> 01:10:32,345
How long before they meet?

1695
01:10:32,345 --> 01:10:36,744
- Oh Gypsy, that is everything
great literature should be,

1696
01:10:36,744 --> 01:10:38,369
according to Merritt Stone.

1697
01:10:38,369 --> 01:10:40,952
- [Tom] He's not Merritt Stone!

1698
01:10:42,047 --> 01:10:45,130
(upbeat dance music)

1699
01:10:48,392 --> 01:10:52,559
(all characters are
arguing at the same time)

1700
01:10:53,411 --> 01:10:54,817
- We could be witnesses.

1701
01:10:54,817 --> 01:10:55,832
- Ladies, please.

1702
01:10:55,832 --> 01:10:57,932
- [Crow] Ladies, back me up on this.

1703
01:10:57,932 --> 01:10:59,162
- [Joel] Merritt Stone,
ladies and gentlemen.

1704
01:10:59,162 --> 01:11:01,580
- [Tom] He's not Merritt Stone.

1705
01:11:01,580 --> 01:11:02,993
- You should have kept the door shut.

1706
01:11:02,993 --> 01:11:04,709
- How'd I know they gonna
be wondering around?

1707
01:11:04,709 --> 01:11:06,497
- Well see that no one else comes in.

1708
01:11:06,497 --> 01:11:07,330
- Yes sir.

1709
01:11:08,799 --> 01:11:13,167
- [Joel] I just told you
not to open the door.

1710
01:11:13,167 --> 01:11:16,087
- Shocking, utterly shocking.

1711
01:11:16,087 --> 01:11:20,830
- Well he tried it before,
this time he made it.

1712
01:11:20,830 --> 01:11:22,275
- Tried what before?

1713
01:11:22,275 --> 01:11:23,281
- Suicide.

1714
01:11:23,281 --> 01:11:24,447
- [Tom] Did it work?

1715
01:11:24,447 --> 01:11:26,919
- [Crow] Old pastrami, canned kraut,

1716
01:11:26,919 --> 01:11:29,666
six bagels bring home for Emma.

1717
01:11:29,666 --> 01:11:30,499
- What makes you

1718
01:11:30,499 --> 01:11:31,954
think it was suicide?
- [Joel] Sit on the evidence,

1719
01:11:31,954 --> 01:11:32,934
why don't ya?

1720
01:11:32,934 --> 01:11:34,001
- Well, what else would it be?

1721
01:11:34,001 --> 01:11:34,834
Murder?

1722
01:11:34,834 --> 01:11:36,241
- [Joel] Well, that's an option.

1723
01:11:36,241 --> 01:11:37,760
- Why do you say that?

1724
01:11:37,760 --> 01:11:39,114
- This note is type written.

1725
01:11:39,114 --> 01:11:39,947
- Well?

1726
01:11:41,147 --> 01:11:43,362
- Where's the typewriter?

1727
01:11:43,362 --> 01:11:44,545
- How well did ya know him, Johnny?

1728
01:11:44,545 --> 01:11:45,506
- Who?

1729
01:11:45,506 --> 01:11:46,645
- The Lelund boy.

1730
01:11:46,645 --> 01:11:48,009
- [Crow] Well, we dated.

1731
01:11:48,009 --> 01:11:49,342
- Casually, why?

1732
01:11:50,544 --> 01:11:52,135
- This has been a funny trip.

1733
01:11:52,135 --> 01:11:54,724
- [Tom] Yeah, sure in
a dream of Gallagher.

1734
01:11:54,724 --> 01:11:57,385
- Well I haven't been splitting my sides.

1735
01:11:57,385 --> 01:11:59,766
- I didn't mean it that way.

1736
01:11:59,766 --> 01:12:00,717
- What are you doin'?

1737
01:12:00,717 --> 01:12:01,898
- What, I'm getting a cigarette.

1738
01:12:01,898 --> 01:12:03,517
- [Joel] Hey don't take my last cigarette.

1739
01:12:03,517 --> 01:12:04,350
- Johnny!

1740
